{[%evp 0,80,28,41,46,44,44,25,49,52,65,19,19,19,19,9,25,28,53,53,58,47,47,45,43,38,65,62,72,72,47,47,73,93,27,45,86,95,112,112,119,120,126,113,133,117,127,89,121,117,147,127,158,112,108,119,149,84,172,160,167,137,174,161,134,103,265,226,299,156,226,231,381,352,476,304,411,260,531,529,544,503,503]} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 e5?! 4. O-O Bd6 {Not 3...h5, of course (which Magnus tried in some other games), but odd enough.} 5. c3 {[%cal Yd2d4] The most logical plan.} a6 6. Ba4 b5 7. Bc2 (7. Bb3 Bb7 8. d4 exd4 9. cxd4 c4 10. Bc2 Nb4 11. Nc3 Nxc2 12. Qxc2 Ne7 $13 {1/2 (48) Xu,Y (2545)-Zhou,W (2588) China 2019}) 7... Nge7 8. d3 {This move is hardly ambitious.} (8. d4 cxd4 9. cxd4 exd4 10. Nxd4 Nxd4 11. Qxd4 Qc7 12. Qd3 Bxh2+ 13. Kh1 Bf4 $13 {1-0 (29) Jones,G (2702)-Vidit,S (2707) Hengshui 2019}) (8. a4!? Rb8 (8... b4 9. d4 cxd4 10. cxd4 exd4 (10... Nxd4 11. Nxd4 exd4 12. Nd2) 11. Nbd2! (11. Nxd4 Nxd4 12. Qxd4 Qc7 13. h3 a5 $13 {1-0 (44) Saydaliev,S (2384)-Nigmatov,O (2447) Tashkent 2020}) 11... Bc5 (11... Qc7!?) 12. Nb3 d6 13. Nfxd4 Ne5 14. Bg5 f6 15. Bh4 O-O 16. f4 N5g6 17. Bg3 $16 {1/2 (38) Mammadova,G (2355)-Khukhashvili,S (2301) Batumi 2018}) 9. axb5 axb5 10. d4 cxd4 11. cxd4 Nxd4 12. Nxd4 exd4 13. Nd2 (13. Qxd4!? Qc7 14. h3) 13... O-O 14. e5 Bxe5 15. Bxh7+ Kxh7 16. Qh5+ Kg8 17. Qxe5 Rb6 {0-1 (44) Bologan,V (2640)-Korobov,A (2695) Poikovsky 2017} 18. Nf3 $14) 8... Ng6 {Preventing Nf3-h4.} (8... O-O 9. Be3 Bb7 10. Nh4 Re8 11. Nd2 Ng6 12. Nf5 Bf8 13. Qg4 $14 {1-0 (57) Caruana,F (2835)-Carlsen,M (2863) lichess.org INT 2020}) 9. Be3 O-O 10. Nbd2 Be7 11. Bb3 d6 {A normal position, quite solid for Black, has arisen.} 12. Bd5 Qe8 (12... Qc7 {was more natural. If} 13. d4 {then} exd4 14. cxd4 Bb7) 13. d4 exd4 14. cxd4 Rb8 15. Rc1 (15. a3 cxd4 16. Nxd4 Nxd4 17. Bxd4 Be6 $11) 15... Nb4!? {[%mdl 512] A correct pawn sacrifice.} (15... c4 $143 ?! 16. Bxc6 Qxc6 17. d5 {[%cal Yb2b3]}) 16. dxc5 dxc5 17. Bxc5 Nxd5 (17... Bxc5 $142 ! 18. Rxc5 Nf4 $44) 18. exd5 Bxc5 19. Rxc5 {Black has no sufficient compensation now.} Bb7 (19... Nf4 20. Re1 Qd8 21. Ne4 $16) 20. Nb3 {This knight had a better route:} (20. Re1 $142 ! Qd7 21. Nf1 Rbd8 22. Ne5 (22. Ne3 $143 Ne7) 22... Qd6 23. Nxg6 fxg6 (23... Qxc5 24. Nxf8 Kxf8 25. Ne3 Bxd5? 26. Qd3 {[%cal Rd3h7,Re1d1]}) 24. Qd4 Rf4 25. Qe3 Rf5 26. Rd1 {, and Black can't regain the pawn.}) 20... Qd7?! (20... Rd8! 21. Na5 Ba8 {[%csl Rd5][%cal Yd8d6,Ye8d7] , and Black should regain the d5 pawn.}) 21. Na5 Ba8 22. Nc6 Rbe8 23. Nfd4 $16 {White has kept his extra pawn and got perfect centralization.} Qd6 24. b4 Re4 25. Qf3 Rfe8 26. Nf5 Qd7 27. g3 h6 28. h4 Kh8 29. Ne3 Kg8 30. Rfc1 Nf8 31. Nf5 Nh7 32. Kg2? (32. Nb8! Qd8 33. Qxe4 Rxe4 34. Rc8 Re8 35. Rxd8 Rxd8 36. Nc6 $18) 32... Kh8? (32... Bb7 $142 $16) 33. Nb8! $18 Qd8 34. Nc6 Qd7 35. Nb8 Qd8 36. Nxa6 Bxd5 37. Nc7 Bb7 38. Nxe8 Re7 39. Qxb7 Rxb7 40. Ned6 Nf8 1-0

