1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 d5 4. Nc3 Bb4 5. cxd5 exd5 6. Bg5 h6 7. Bh4 Nbd7 8. e3 g5 (8... c5 {including the moves ...h6 and h4, the line is considered as a risky one. However some players disagree with this.} 9. Bd3 Qa5 (9... c4 10. Bf5 Nb6 11. Bc2 Qe7 12. Nd2?! (12. O-O O-O 13. Ne5 $14) 12... O-O 13. O-O Re8 14. a3 Bxc3 15. bxc3 Qe6 16. Bxf6 Qxf6 17. a4 Bf5 18. Bxf5 Qxf5 19. Qb1 Qd7 $11 {Chiburdanidze,M (2502)-Zhao,X (2474) 1/2 (25) Antakya 2010}) 10. Qc2 g5 11. Bg3 c4 12. Bf5 O-O 13. O-O Re8 14. h4 Bxc3 15. bxc3 Ne4 16. hxg5 hxg5 17. Bxe4 dxe4 18. Nd2 $16 {Sargissian,G (2683)-Hanley,C (2421) 1-0 (49) Caleta 2012 CBM 147 [Let's Check]}) 9. Bg3 Ne4 10. Nd2 (10. Qc2 Nb6 11. Bd3 Nxg3 12. hxg3 Be6 13. Ne5 (13. a3!? Bd6 14. Nb5 $14) 13... Qe7 14. f4 O-O-O 15. O-O Kb8 16. a3 Bd6 17. a4 gxf4 18. gxf4 Rhg8 $13 {Lysyj,I (2648)-Aronian,L (2813) 0-1 (50) Tromso 2013}) 10... Nxg3 (10... Nxc3 {is too bold:} 11. bxc3 Bxc3 12. Rc1 Ba5 13. h4 {and Black is in danger.}) 11. fxg3 $146 {With a very unusual pawn structure. In this game Black can't complain about the result of the opening but I wouldn't be in any hurry to claim that 11.fxg3 is a dubious move. We need more games to establish the objective value of this move.} (11. hxg3 Nb6 (11... c6 12. Bd3 Nb6 13. Qc2 Be6 14. O-O-O Qf6 15. f4 O-O-O 16. Nf3 Kb8 17. Kb1 Qg7 18. Rhe1?! (18. f5 Bc8 19. g4 Rhe8 20. e4 $13) 18... Rhe8 19. Re2 Bg4 $15 {Kryakvin,D (2588)-Khismatullin, D (2674) 1/2 (141) Taganrog RUS 2014} (19... f6!?)) 12. a3 Bd6 (12... Bf8 13. Bd3 c6 14. Qc2 Be6 15. O-O-O Qe7 16. Nb3 O-O-O 17. Nc5 Kb8 18. Kb1 Bg7 19. Rc1 h5 $11 {L'Ami,E (2646)-Panjwani,R (2440) 1-0 (38) Reykjavik ISL 2014}) 13. Qc2 c6 14. e4 dxe4 15. Ndxe4 Be6 16. O-O-O Qe7 17. Nxd6+ Qxd6 18. Ne4 Qe7 19. Qc5 Qxc5+ 20. dxc5 Nd7 21. Nxg5 (21. Nd6+ Ke7 22. Nxb7 a5 $11) 21... Bd5 22. Nh3 (22. b4!? a5 23. Bd3 axb4 24. axb4 $14 Bxg2?! 25. Rhe1+ Kf8 26. Bc4 $40) 22... Nxc5 23. Nf4 Bb3 24. Re1+ {1/2 (24) Ragger,M (2680)-Vitiugov,N (2719) Tromso 2013}) 11... Nb6 12. Bd3 Qe7 13. Qf3 Be6 14. a3 {Magnus hurries to exchange the bishop. His king might be well-placed on f2, where it protects the e3-pawn.} (14. O-O O-O-O 15. Rac1 Kb8 16. a3 Bxc3 17. Rxc3 Na4 18. Rc2 Bg4 19. Qf2 Rhe8 20. Re1 Nb6 $15) 14... Bxc3 15. bxc3 O-O-O ({It was not bad to play} 15... O-O!? 16. O-O f5 17. h4 Rae8 18. Rae1 Kg7 $11 {then Black can play ...c8, ...d6.}) 16. a4 Bd7 (16... Kb8 17. a5 Nc8 18. Nb3 Nd6 19. Nc5 $14) ({But} 16... a5?! {is too risky:} 17. O-O ({Black is counting on} 17. Nb3 Rhe8 18. Nxa5 Kb8 19. O-O Bg4 $15) 17... Kb8 18. Nb3 Bc8 19. Qf2! (19. Nxa5 Rhe8 20. Rfe1 (20. Rae1 Qa3) 20... Rd6 21. Nb3 Rf6 22. Qe2 Re6 23. Nc5 Rxe3 24. Qxe3 Qxe3+ 25. Rxe3 Rxe3 26. Kf2 Re7 27. Rb1 Ka7 $11) 19... Rhe8 20. Rae1 Nxa4 (20... Qa3?? 21. Nc5 $18 {with following a1}) 21. Nxa5 Rd6 (21... Nxc3?? 22. Qb2) 22. c4 $40) 17. a5 ({It is worth considering the sacrifice of the a-pawn:} 17. O-O!? Nxa4?! ({I would prefer} 17... Kb8! 18. a5 Na4 19. c4?! Nb2 20. Qe2 Rhe8 $15) 18. c4 $44 Qb4 19. Qf2 Kb8 20. cxd5 f5 21. Nf3 $16) 17... Na4 18. a6 Rhe8 ({He could have played} 18... b5!? 19. O-O Rhe8 {The position is very complicated. White has several options.} 20. Rfe1! (20. e4 Nxc3 21. e5 Qb4 22. Qe3 c5 23. dxc5 Be6 24. Rac1 d4 25. Qf3 Bd5 26. Be4 Nxe4 27. Nxe4 Rxe5 28. Nd6+ Kc7 29. Qd3 Rxd6 30. cxd6+ Kxd6 $13 {with a very messy position.}) 20... Nxc3 21. Rac1 Ne4 22. Nb3 $44) 19. Kf2 Kb8 {Threatening ...g4.} 20. Rhe1 $8 (20. axb7?? Bg4 $19) 20... Nxc3 21. axb7 Qb4! $132 22. Kg1 (22. Nf1 {allows Black to play} c5! 23. Kg1 (23. dxc5?? Bg4 $19) 23... cxd4 24. Kh1 Re6 $15 25. Qxf7 Qf8 26. Qxf8 Rxf8 27. exd4 Rxe1 28. Rxe1 a5 $17 {The a-pawn is very dangerous.}) 22... Qb2 23. Nf1 ({There is no relief after} 23. Qf2 Re6 24. Rac1 Rde8 25. Nf3 Qxf2+ 26. Kxf2 Ne4+ 27. Bxe4 dxe4 28. Ne5 Bb5 29. Rc5 a6 $15) 23... f5 24. Ra5?! (24. Rac1! {intending c2 and ec1} Ba4 (24... Ne4?! 25. Rc2 Qb3 26. Qe2 Re6 27. Rec1 $14) 25. Bxf5 Rf8 26. g4 Rd6 27. Ng3 $13) 24... Ba4 {Black should not be afraid of ea1.} (24... Rf8 25. Qf2 (25. Rea1?! Ba4 26. Re1 f4 27. gxf4 gxf4 28. exf4 Qb4 $17) 25... Qxf2+ 26. Kxf2 f4 27. gxf4 gxf4 28. Kg1 Bf5 29. Bxf5 Rxf5 30. Rea1 Rd6 31. Rxa7 Nb5 $11) 25. Rc5?! ({I think he should have preferred} 25. Qf2 Qb4 26. Ra6 f4 27. gxf4 gxf4 28. Qxf4 Bb5 29. Bxb5 Qxb5 30. Qxh6 Ne2+ 31. Kh1 Nxd4 {A complex position with approximately equal chances.}) (25. Bxf5 Rf8 26. g4 Rd6) 25... Rf8 26. h3 Rf6 27. Nh2 Rdf8 $15 28. Qf1 Ne4 29. Re2? (29. Rxd5 Nxg3 30. Qf2 Qc3 31. Qxg3 Qxd3 $15) 29... Qa3! 30. Bxe4 fxe4 $17 {Magnus' position is very difficult, after ...xb7 his opponent gets a material advantage, the knight on h2 will be out of play after ...h5.} 31. Qe1 c6 32. Ra5 Qb3?! (32... h5! 33. g4 h4 {and White has no useful moves. Black's position is winning.}) 33. Qa1 Qd1+? {Now White is on top.} (33... Bb5 34. Ra3 Qxa3 35. Qxa3 Bxe2 36. Qb2 Bd3 $17 37. Ng4 (37. Qa3 h5) 37... Rf1+ 38. Kh2 Rb1 $19) 34. Qxd1 Bxd1 35. Re1 Bh5 $8 (35... Bb3 36. Ng4 $16) 36. g4 Be8 37. Rea1 Rf2?! (37... Kxb7 38. Rxa7+ Kb6 39. R7a6+ Kc7 40. Nf1 $14 {Black needs to play precisely to draw.}) 38. Rxa7 Rb2 39. Nf1 $16 Kc7 (39... Rxb7 40. Ra8+ Kc7 41. Ng3 {Due to the deadly pin, White is winning.}) 40. Ra8 Kxb7 41. R1a7+ Kb6 42. Re7 Rbf2 43. Rb8+! (43. Ng3?! {is much weaker:} Bg6 44. Rxf8 Rxf8 45. Re6 Rg8 {Black has good chances to make a draw. For example} 46. Nf5 Bxf5 47. gxf5 Rf8 48. g4 Rh8 49. Kf2 Kb5 $14) 43... Ka6 44. Ng3 Bg6 45. Rxf8 Rxf8 46. Re6 Be8 (46... Rg8 47. Rxc6+ $18) 47. Rxh6 Kb5 {The king is the most active black piece.} 48. Rh7 {It seems that Magnus could win immediately after 48.d6:} (48. Rd6! Kc4 (48... Kb6 49. Nf5 Kc7 50. Rh6 Bd7 51. Rh7 Kd8 52. Nd6 $18) 49. Nf5 Kd3 50. Rd8 Ke2 51. h4 gxh4 52. Kh2 Kf2 53. Kh3 Rh8 54. g5 $18) 48... Kc4 49. Ra7 Bg6 50. Ra6 Rf6 51. Ra3! Kb4 52. Ra1 Kc3 53. Rf1 Re6 54. Rf8 Kd2 {This gives White a tempo.} (54... Kd3! 55. Nf1 c5 56. dxc5 Rc6 $16 57. Rf2 (57. Ra8 Rxc5 58. Ra3+ Rc3 59. Rxc3+? Kxc3 $11) 57... Rxc5 58. Rd2+ Kc3 59. Rd4 $16) 55. Nf1+ Kd3 (55... Ke2! 56. Rf2+ Kd3 57. Rf8 c5 58. dxc5 Rc6 59. Rf2 Rxc5 60. Rd2+ Kc3 61. Rd4 $16 {leads to the above mentioned position.}) 56. Kf2 Re7 57. Rg8 Re6 (57... Bh7 58. Ra8! $16 ({With a little trap} 58. Rxg5? Rf7+ 59. Ke1 Ra7 60. h4 Ra2 61. Rg7 Re2+ 62. Kd1 Rf2 $11)) 58. Ke1 Rf6 59. Rg7 Re6 60. Ra7 Re8 61. Ra3+! Kc2 62. Ra6 Rc8 63. Ke2 Be8 64. Ra5 Kc3?! (64... c5 65. Rxc5+? {leads to a draw} (65. dxc5 Kc3 66. Ng3 Kb4 67. Ra7 Rxc5 68. Nf5 $16) 65... Rxc5 66. dxc5 Bb5+ 67. Ke1 Bxf1 68. Kxf1 d4 69. c6 Kd2! $11) ({The best chance was} 64... Rb8! 65. Rc5+ Kb3 66. Ng3 (66. Nd2+! Kb4 67. Kd1 Ra8 68. Nb1 Ra1 69. Kc1 $16) 66... Ra8 67. Nh5 Ra2+ 68. Kf1 Ra7 69. Kg1 Ra1+ 70. Kf2 Ra2+ 71. Kg3 Rc2! 72. Ra5 (72. Rxc2? Kxc2 73. Nf6 c5!! 74. dxc5 (74. Nxe8 cxd4 $19) 74... Bc6 75. Kf2 d4 76. exd4 Kd2 77. Nxe4+ Bxe4 78. g3 Kd3 $11) 72... c5 73. Nf6 Bc6 74. dxc5 Kb4 $14) 65. Ng3 Rb8 66. Rc5+! Kb2 67. Nh5 $18 {Black's position is hopeless.} Bxh5 68. gxh5 Rh8 69. g4 Rh6 70. Kf2 Re6 71. Kg3 Rf6 72. h4! Rf3+ 73. Kg2 gxh4 74. h6 Rxe3 75. h7 h3+ 76. Kh2 Re2+ 77. Kxh3 Re1 78. Kg2 Re2+ 79. Kg3 Re3+ 80. Kh4 Re1 81. Kg5 Rh1 82. Kg6 Rh4 83. Rxc6 e3 84. Re6 Rxg4+ 85. Kh5 Rg1 86. Rxe3 Rh1+ 87. Kg6 Rg1+ 88. Kf7 Rh1 89. Kg8 Rg1+ 90. Kh8 Rg4 91. Re5 Rxd4 92. Kg7 Rg4+ 93. Kh6 1-0

