1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nc3 dxc4 {Hikaru tried this line recently against Mamedyarov in the Olympiad.} 4. e3 b5 5. a4 b4 6. Ne4 Qd5 7. Nd2 c3 8. bxc3 {Mamedyarov played 8.Ndf3. For some reason, Hikaru was either unfamiliar with this line (the main line) or forgot his analysis.} bxc3 9. Nb1 Qa5 10. Qc2 {This is a common position. Black usually plays 10...Na6. Hikaru went into a long think, and played an interesting move.} e5!? 11. Nf3 {And now Hikaru thought for a long time, and made the losing move.} Na6?? (11... exd4 12. Nxd4 Nf6 {is better for white, but the game goes on. Perhaps Hikaru thought this was too simple and played for complications, but they were not in his favor.}) 12. Nxe5 {Black is simply lost. He will be 1-2 pawns in the ending with no compensation.} Nb4 {Played after long thought, but there is nothing else.} 13. Qb3! Be6 14. Bc4 c2?! (14... Bxc4 15. Qxc4 Qd5 (15... Nc2+? 16. Kd1 Nxa1 17. Qxf7+ Kd8 18. Qd7#) 16. O-O {is best, but white should be winning.}) 15. Bxe6 Nd3+ 16. Ke2 Nxe5 17. dxe5 fxe6 18. Qxe6+ Ne7 19. Nd2 Qd5 {The computer says this is best, but black has little chance of survival in the ending.} 20. Qxd5 Nxd5 21. Ne4 Rb8 22. Bd2 Bb4 23. Rhc1 Bxd2 24. Nxd2 Nb4 25. Nf3 Ke7 26. Ne1 Rhd8 27. f4! (27. Nxc2?! Nd3 28. Rcb1 Nxe5 {is great for white, but not completely winning.}) 27... c5 28. Nxc2 Nd3 29. Rcb1 Nb2 30. Ra2 Nxa4 {A bit tricky, but unfortunately, not tricky enough.} 31. Rxb8 Nc3+ 32. Kf3 Nxa2 33. Rb5 Nb4 34. Nxb4 cxb4 35. Rxb4 Ra8 36. Ke4 a5 37. Ra4 Kf7 38. g4 Ke7 39. f5 h6 40. h4 Kf7 41. e6+ Kf6 42. Rd4 Ke7 (42... Ra7 43. g5+ hxg5 44. Rd7 Rxd7 45. exd7 Ke7 46. f6+ gxf6 47. h5 {is a funny computer line.}) 43. Rd7+ Kf8 44. e7+ Ke8 45. Rd8+ Rxd8 46. exd8=Q+ Kxd8 47. Kd5 Ke7 48. g5 a4 49. Kc4 hxg5 50. hxg5 Kd6 51. e4 Ke5 52. Kb4 1-0

