{[%evp 0,89,26,26,25,-23,-9,-9,0,0,25,12,18,-26,-37,-48,-13,-12,-23,-23,-18,-28,-23,-10,8,-28,-18,-32,-31,-33,-12,5,-46,-35,-19,-71,-19,-88,21,-6,0,0,45,8,-7,-7,-2,3,36,37,42,68,106,75,120,117,136,127,127,91,202,167,375,230,230,230,96,79,90,78,100,79,107,103,108,94,113,122,122,105,109,24,219,229,235,258,317,371,358,371,416,656]} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 d5 4. Nc3 c6 5. Bg5 h6 6. Bh4 dxc4 7. e4 g5 8. Bg3 b5 9. Be2 b4 {A rare move. Black usually plays 9...b7, 9...bd7 or sometimes 9...g7.} 10. Na4 Nxe4 11. Be5! Nf6 (11... f6? 12. Qc2! $16) 12. Nc5!? {One of the critical moves according to theory. Several moves have been tried and plenty of things are left to be discovered.} (12. Rc1 {was tried by Vidit, and after} Bg7?! (12... Nbd7!?) 13. Nc5 Nbd7 14. Nxd7 Qxd7 15. h4 g4 16. Nd2 Ba6 17. Bxg4 c3 18. bxc3 bxc3 19. Nb3 Qd5 20. Bf3 Qc4 {he got a wonderful position until he played the slightly unfortunate} 21. Rh3?? {allowing} Qf1# {0-1 Vidit,S (2643)-Hovhannisyan,R (2611) ARM 2015.}) (12. h4 g4 13. Nd2 Nbd7 (13... c3!? 14. bxc3 Nbd7 15. O-O Nxe5 16. dxe5 Nd7 17. Ne4 Nxe5 $132 {1-0 (32) Aloma Vidal,R (2433)-Sadek,S (2316) Tirana ALB 2018}) 14. Nxc4 Ba6 15. Qc2 Bxc4 16. Qxc4 Rc8 17. Rc1 Nxe5 18. dxe5 Nd7 19. Qxg4 Nxe5 $132 {½-½ (79) Vitiugov,N (2691)-Hovhannisyan,R (2610) St Petersburg 2012}) (12. Bxc4 {has been played the more often:} Nbd7 (12... g4!?) 13. O-O g4 14. Nd2 Nxe5 15. dxe5 Nd7 16. Re1!? (16. Qxg4 Nxe5 17. Qe2 Bg7 18. Rad1 O-O 19. f4 Nxc4 20. Nxc4 $13 {0-1 (43) Antic,D (2505)-Lajthajm,B (2464) Pancevo 2006}) 16... Qa5 17. Bb3 Nxe5 18. Ne4 Bg7 19. Qd6 Qd8 20. Qxb4 Qe7? (20... Nd3! 21. Nd6+ Kf8! 22. Qa3 c5! $13) 21. Nd6+ Kf8 22. Rad1 $18 {1-0 (51) Lalith,B (2484)-Debashis,D (2389) Moscow 2012}) 12... c3 {The best move according to the engine.} (12... Bd6 13. Bxc4 a5 14. O-O O-O 15. Qe2 $14 {1-0 (35) Stocek,J (2584)-Voloshin,L (2437) Pardubice 2009}) 13. bxc3 bxc3 14. O-O Nbd7?! $146 (14... g4 {looks critical:} 15. Qb3!? (15. Ne1!? $146 Bxc5 16. dxc5 Qxd1 17. Rxd1 Ke7 {and here I'm not sure White has much better than a draw with d6-e5, but he has many playable moves.}) (15. Qa4!? $146 gxf3 16. Bxf3 Bxc5 17. dxc5 {would also give White plenty of compensaton according to the engine! Perhaps we'll see that in a future game.}) 15... Bxc5 16. dxc5 Nbd7 (16... gxf3 17. Bxf3 $44) 17. Rfd1 O-O (17... gxf3 18. Bxf3 $16) (17... Rg8!?) 18. Ne1 Nd5 19. Bd6 f5 $13 {1-0 (53) Ragger,M (2680)-Hovhannisyan,R (2623) ARM 2013}) 15. Nxd7 Bxd7 16. Qb3 Bg7 17. Qa3 (17. Qxc3) 17... g4 18. Ne1 c5?! (18... Qe7! 19. Bd6 Qd8 {seemed better, as} 20. Qxc3? {is met with} Ne4 $17) 19. dxc5! $14 (19. Qxc5 Ne4 20. Qa3 Bxe5 21. dxe5 Qe7 $17) 19... O-O 20. Bxc3 h5 21. Rd1 Nd5 (21... Qe7 22. Be5!? $14 (22. f3!? $14)) 22. Bxg7 Kxg7 23. Bc4 Bc6 24. Nc2 Qf6 25. Nd4 Ne7 26. f3! g3 {Black cannot afford to open the f-file.} 27. hxg3 Rfd8 28. Nxc6 Nxc6 29. Qe3 Nd4?! (29... Rab8 $142 $16) 30. g4! Rac8 (30... hxg4? 31. fxg4 $18) 31. g5 Qf5! (31... Qe7 32. Qe5+ f6 33. gxf6+ Qxf6 34. Rde1 $18) 32. Rxd4! {The rook ending is a safe bet for White!} (32. Ba6 Rc6 33. Bb7 Rc7 34. c6 e5 35. Rc1 Rd6 $132) 32... Qxc5 33. Bxe6! Rc6 (33... fxe6 34. Rfd1 $16) 34. Re4 Qxe3+ 35. Rxe3 Rxe6 (35... fxe6 {may have been a smarter defence, given what happened in the game with one pair of rooks left.}) 36. Rxe6 fxe6 37. Re1 Rd6 38. Kh2 Kg6 39. f4 Kf5 (39... h4 40. g4! $18) 40. Kg3 h4+? {This makes White's task easier, but the position was lost anyway.} (40... Rd3+ {was the only chance, but it loses.} 41. Kh4 Rd2 (41... Kxf4 42. Rf1+ Ke5 43. g6 $18) 42. Kxh5! (42. Re5+ Kxf4 43. Rxe6 Rxg2 44. Rf6+ Ke5 45. Kxh5 {transposes}) 42... Rxg2 43. Kh6 Rxa2 44. Re5+ Kxf4 45. Rxe6 {Black isn't in time with his a-pawn.} Kf5 (45... a5 46. g6 Ra3 47. Kh7 Kg5 (47... Kf5 48. Ra6 $18) 48. g7 Rh3+ 49. Kg8 Rf3 50. Re5+ Kf6 51. Rxa5 $18) (45... Rh2+ 46. Kg6 Rg2 47. Rf6+ Ke5 48. Ra6 $18) 46. Rf6+ Ke5 47. Kg7 a5 48. g6 a4 49. Kf7 $18) 41. Kxh4 Kxf4 42. g6 Rd8 43. Rf1+ Ke3 44. Kg5 e5 45. g7 1-0

