{[%evp 0,47,16,13,30,27,30,29,48,27,88,32,46,-13,14,8,36,27,17,16,10,8,18,5,0,18,34,-27,-12,0,16,-30,-2,26,30,30,23,4,29,-11,148,104,137,156,247,249,256,256,264,288]} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 d5 3. Bf4 c5 4. e3 e6 5. c3 Bd6 6. Nbd2!? cxd4 {With this move order, Black tries to force White to take back with the c-pawn, but...} (6... Nc6 {is the main move.}) (6... Bxf4 7. exf4 cxd4 {would allow} 8. Nxd4 Nc6 9. N2f3 {with a slightly favourable pawn structure for White.}) 7. Bxd6!? dxe3 (7... Qxd6 8. exd4 {is the type of position Magnus was surely hoping for.}) (7... dxc3 8. Ba3 cxd2+ 9. Nxd2 Nc6 10. Bb5 {would give White similar compensation to that in the game - although I prefer this version for Black.}) 8. Ba3 exd2+ 9. Qxd2 Nc6 ({Maybe Black should have tried something more active:} 9... Ne4!? 10. Qd4 (10. Qf4!?) 10... f6 11. Bd3 Nc6 12. Qe3 Qb6 13. Qe2 Nc5 14. Bc2 e5 $132) 10. Qg5! {Highlighting Black's problems on the dark squares.} Rg8 (10... g6 11. Bd3 $44) 11. Bd3 h6 12. Qe3 Qb6 13. Qe2 Bd7 14. O-O O-O-O {Black manages to castle - but not on the side he wishes. White's compensation is obvious.} 15. b4 (15. c4!?) 15... Kb8 ({It was the last moment for Black to seek for some freedom with} 15... e5! 16. Nxe5 (16. b5 e4 17. bxc6 Bxc6 18. Nd4 exd3 19. Qxd3 Qc7 $13) 16... Nxe5 17. Qxe5 Rge8 18. Qf4 Ng4!? {followed by ...e5 or ...g5, and Black's activity should compensate for the bishop pair.}) 16. b5! Na5 17. Ne5 Be8 18. Bb4 {Black has an extra pawn but he's paralyzed.} Rc8 19. a4 (19. Rac1!? {with the idea of 20.c4 also looked very strong.}) 19... Ne4? {A bad decision in a bad position. Black should maybe have chosen a waiting move like ...c7 or ...a8, but White was soon going to push c4 and would have remained better.} (19... Nb3 20. Rab1 Nc5 {would allow} 21. Nc6+! $16 {with the idea of a5.}) 20. Bxe4 dxe4 21. Qxe4 f6 (21... f5 22. Qd3 $18) 22. Qh7! {Simple chess! White collects the g8-rook.} Nb3 (22... Bh5? 23. Nd7+ $18) 23. Qxg8 Nxa1 24. Qxe8! (24. Qxe8 Rxe8 25. Nd7+ Kc7 26. Nxb6 axb6 27. Rxa1 $18) 1-0

