{[%evp 0,61,25,25,26,-9,38,-20,13,8,16,-6,25,22,12,9,37,38,52,36,55,50,47,42,40,47,52,5,65,43,43,21,66,39,42,25,25,35,-2,-22,-4,-4,-4,-4,47,35,59,88,88,-22,-3,44,44,-214,-218,2,161,458,29995,29996,29997,29998,29999,-30000]} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. g3 Bg7 4. Bg2 O-O 5. Nc3 d6 6. Nf3 Nc6 7. O-O e5 8. d5 Ne7 9. e4 b6 {A rare move compared to 9...d7 and 9...e8.} 10. Rb1 a5 11. Re1!? {A prophylactic move to play a3 without allowing ...a4 (as after xa4 the e4-pawn would be protected).} Nd7 (11... Bd7 12. b3 {followed by a3 and b4 would leave Black without a serious plan.}) 12. a3 h6 13. Nh4! f5 (13... g5 14. Nf5 Nxf5 15. exf5 $16) 14. exf5 gxf5 15. Qc2 Nf6 16. b4 {White got a perfect position: all of his pieces are on the best possible square, particularily the knight on h4.} Bd7 17. c5! axb4 18. axb4 e4?! (18... Qe8 19. c6 Bc8 {followed by ...f7 was a better defence.}) 19. c6 Be8 20. f3! {Taking advantage of Black's 18th move. Now the position will open and Black is definitely not in the best situation for it.} Nfxd5 (20... exf3 21. Bxf3 $16) 21. Nxd5 Nxd5 22. fxe4 fxe4 23. Bxe4? (23. Rxe4! Nc3 24. Rg4 Nxb1 25. Bxh6 Rf7 26. Bd5 $18) 23... Nc3? (23... Bd4+! 24. Kh1 Nc3 {was the correct move order:} 25. Bb2 (25. Qd3 Qf6 26. Bb2 Nxe4 27. Rxe4 Bxb2 28. Rg4+ Kh8 29. Ng6+ Bxg6 30. Rxg6 Qf5 31. Qxf5 Rxf5 32. Rxb2 $11) (25. Bxh6 Rf2 26. Qd3 Qf6 27. Bg5 Qxg5 28. Qxd4 Nxe4 29. Qxe4 Bf7 30. Kg1 $13) (25. Rb3 Rf2) 25... Rf2 26. Qd3 Qf6 27. Bd5+ Kf8 $13) 24. Bxh6! Qf6 (24... Bd4+ {now allows} 25. Be3! Qf6 26. Rbc1 {and Black is in trouble. A fun line goes} Ra2 27. Bd5+ Nxd5 28. Qxa2 Bxe3+ 29. Rxe3 Qd4 30. Ng2 Kg7 31. Qc4 Qxc4 32. Rxc4 Nxe3 33. Nxe3 b5 {and Black has drawing chances.}) (24... Bxh6? 25. Qxc3 $18) (24... Qf6 25. Bh7+! Kh8 26. Rxe8! Bxh6 27. Re7! Bg7 28. Rbe1 Qd4+ 29. Kh1 Qd5+ 30. Be4 Nxe4 31. Ng6+ Kg8 32. R7xe4 Rf7 33. Nf4 $18) (24... Nxe4 25. Bxg7 Kxg7 26. Rxe4 $18) 25. Bh7+! Kh8 26. Rxe8! Rfxe8? (26... Bxh6 27. Re7!? Rf7 28. Rxf7 Qxf7 29. Qxc3+ Kxh7 30. Qd3+ Kh8 31. Re1 $18) 27. Ng6+! Kxh7 28. Nf8+ Kxh6 (28... Kg8 29. Qh7+ Kxf8 (29... Kf7 30. Rf1 $18) 30. Bxg7+ Qxg7 31. Rf1+ $18) 29. Qh7+ Kg5 30. Qh4+ Kf5 31. Qf4# {A nice finish!} 1-0

