{[%evp 0,58,19,38,41,14,47,68,68,64,74,62,76,42,33,51,44,35,35,14,41,12,1,14,14,20,27,17,18,2,24,52,89,58,58,63,45,33,98,86,218,64,332,81,196,181,246,239,342,366,323,347,474,515,511,621,621,641,636,643,1526]} 1. e4 Nc6 2. Nf3 {Changing from 2.d4, as in the previous game. Black has several possibilities here: 2...d6 (playing some sort of Pirc Defence when White already played f3), 2...e5 (transposing into 1.e4 e5 2.f3 c6), or the Scandinavian way as in the game.} d5 3. exd5 Qxd5 4. Nc3 Qa5 5. d4 Bg4 6. Bb5 O-O-O 7. Bxc6 bxc6 8. h3 Qh5 9. Be3!? (9. Qe2 {can lead to very weird games:} Bxf3 10. gxf3 e6 11. Ne4 Rxd4 12. Be3 Qa5+ 13. c3 Ra4 14. O-O Qb5 15. Qc2 Nf6 16. b3 Ra5 17. b4 Qa4 18. Qe2 Rh5 19. Ng3 Rxh3 20. Kg2 Rh4 21. Bg5 Nd5 22. Rfd1 h6 23. Rxd5 Rh2+! {0-1 Riff,J (2469)-Bauer,C (2625) SUI 2009}) 9... Nf6 (9... Bxf3 10. gxf3 e5 11. Qe2! exd4 12. Qa6+ Kb8 13. O-O-O Qc5 14. Qa4 $16 {1-0 (30) Muzychuk,A (2558)-Zhao Xue (2504) Doha 2016}) 10. Qe2 Bxf3 11. gxf3 e6 12. O-O-O Kb7 13. Rhg1! $146 (13. Rd3 Rb8 14. Rg1 h6?! 15. Bf4 Qf5 16. Be5 $16 {0-1 (56) Guseinov,G (2613)-Bacrot,E (2720) Dubai 2014}) 13... h6 (13... Qxh3 14. Ne4 Nd5 15. Kb1 Rb8 16. c4 Nxe3 17. fxe3 $40) (13... Nd5 14. Ne4 $40) (13... Qa5 14. Kb1 h6 15. Ne4 $14) 14. Rd3! {Let's be clear: Ding is just crushing Carlsen's line.} Rg8?! {Difficult to think of a worse move, as after White's next move, the knight on f6 will be hanging.} (14... Rb8 $142) 15. Ne4 Be7 (15... Nxe4 16. Rb3+ Kc8 17. Qa6+ Kd7 18. fxe4 $18) 16. Rb3+ Kc8 17. Qa6+ Kd7 18. Rd1! Qxf3 (18... Qf5 19. d5! exd5 (19... cxd5 20. Qa4+ $18) (19... Nxd5 20. c4 $18) 20. Rc3 Qe6 21. Bxa7 Ra8 22. Qb7 $18) 19. Nd2 (19. d5!! {was a crusher:} exd5 (19... Nxd5 20. Nc5+! Bxc5 21. Bxc5 Qf4+ 22. Be3 Qd6 23. c4 $18) (19... cxd5 20. Qa4+ c6 21. Rb7+ Ke8 22. Nxf6+ Qxf6 23. Qxc6+ Kf8 24. Rxe7! $18) 20. Rc3! Ke8 21. Qxc6+ Kf8 22. Nxf6 Qxf6 23. Qxc7 $18) 19... Qxh3? (19... Qd5 {was necessary, but Black's position remains terrible.}) 20. Nc4! Ke8 21. Ne5 Bd6 22. Nxc6 Ra8 23. Qb7 Kd7 24. Ne5+ Ke7 25. Bf4! {The game is over.} Qf5 26. Nc6+ Kd7 27. Bxd6 Kxd6 28. Ne5 Qf4+ 29. Kb1 Rgf8 1-0

