1. e4 c6 2. Nf3 d5 3. Nc3 Qa5 {Magnus is definitely having fun!} (3... Bg4 {or 3...dxe4 or 3...Nf6 are the usual answers.}) 4. Be2 dxe4 (4... Bg4 5. h3 Bxf3 6. Bxf3 e6 7. O-O $16 {½-½ (65) Shahade,G (2476)-Trent,L (2398) chess.com 2022}) 5. Nxe4 Bf5 6. Ng3 Bg6 7. O-O Nd7 8. d4 e6 9. Nh4 $146 (9. Bf4 {is usually being played.}) 9... Bd6?! {Black had to get rid off the tension on the kingside.} (9... Be7 10. Nxg6 hxg6 11. c4 Ngf6 $132) 10. c4 Qd8 {Going back to d8 was probably not the idea behind 3...Qa5!} (10... Ngf6 11. f4 $40) 11. Nxg6?! (11. d5! {right away was stronger! A knight could potencially jump to f5 while} Qxh4? 12. dxe6 {is just terrible for Black.}) 11... hxg6 12. d5! Qh4 13. h3 exd5? {A terrible positionnal mistake.} (13... cxd5 14. cxd5 e5 {was wiser, although after} 15. Qb3 Ngf6 16. Be3! {White seems to be better.} (16. Qxb7? Rb8 17. Qc6 Bc5! $132)) 14. cxd5 c5 15. a4!? {Objectively not the best, but this move definitely deserves an interesting mark for the ideas it hides: bringing the a-rook into play!} (15. Bg4 Ngf6 16. Re1+ {looked awful for Black.}) 15... a5? {Again a terrible move positionally speaking, but Magnus was surely worried about a5 and Ra4, and for good reason!} (15... Ngf6 {was anyway the best way to go, and after} 16. a5 {Black can play 16...c4 or 16...Qd4 and is not entirely lost.}) (15... Bxg3? 16. fxg3 Qxg3 17. Ra3 $18) 16. Bb5 Nf6 17. Re1+ Kd8 18. Ra3! Re8 19. Rxe8+ (19. Bd2!?) 19... Kxe8 20. Rc3 {Splending manoeuvre!} Kd8 (20... Qd4 {was the only way to put up some resistance.}) 21. Rc4 Qh8 {Outch! That's really a bad sign if you need to play such a move.} 22. Bg5 Nb6 (22... Kc7 23. Bxd7 Kxd7 24. Qb3 Kc7 25. Bxf6 gxf6 26. Ne4 $18) 23. Rh4! {The danse continues!} Qf8 24. Ne4 {it is all over.} Kc8 25. Nxf6 (25. Nxd6+!? Qxd6 26. Qf3 $18) 25... gxf6 26. Bxf6 Kc7 27. Qd2 Qc8 28. Rh7 Qg8 29. Rh8 Qxh8 30. Bxh8 Rxh8 31. Qxa5 Rh4 32. Qe1 Nd7 33. g3 Rh8 34. Qa5+ Nb6 35. Qc3 Rxh3 36. Qg7 1-0

