{[%evp 0,63,29,29,32,-9,33,42,35,32,32,10,21,9,13,22,15,-2,32,23,30,30,20,-6,4,7,28,32,33,7,17,30,17,17,29,-85,-49,-120,-37,0,12,39,114,115,138,133,130,128,134,142,155,103,106,124,124,126,182,185,181,172,192,191,192,195,194,196]} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. e3 Nf6 4. Nc3 Bf5 5. Nf3 e6 6. Nh4 Be4 7. f3 Bg6 8. Bd2 Be7 (8... Nbd7 {is Black's other main option.}) 9. Nxg6 hxg6 10. Qb3 Qc7 (10... Qb6 11. Qxb6 axb6 12. Kf2 $14) 11. O-O-O! {It is difficult to come up with another move here. As long as Black's knight stands on b8, exchanging pawns on d5 isn't a great idea due to ...cxd5 and ...c6.} dxc4 (11... a6 {should be critical, I believe. White has several options:} 12. Kb1!? (12. g4!?) (12. c5!? Nbd7 13. Kb1 b6 14. cxb6 Nxb6 15. h4 a5 16. Qc2 a4 17. e4 Qb7 18. a3 $36) (12. cxd5 cxd5 13. Kb1 Nc6 14. Ne2 b5 15. Rc1 Qb6 $11 {1-0 (67) Ghaem Maghami,E (2596)-Schneider,I (2481) Berlin 2015}) 12... dxc4 (12... b5 13. cxd5 cxd5 14. Rc1 $14) 13. Qxc4 b5 14. Qd3 Nbd7 (14... c5 15. dxc5 Nbd7 16. b4 $14) 15. e4 $44) 12. Bxc4 b5 13. Be2 a6 14. Ne4! (14. Kb1 c5 15. dxc5 Nbd7 $11) 14... Nxe4 (14... O-O 15. Nxf6+ Bxf6 16. Kb1 Nd7 17. Rc1 $14) 15. fxe4 c5 16. Kb1 Nc6 (16... Nd7 17. h4! {is also quite unpleasant for Black.} (17. e5!?)) (16... c4 17. Qc2 Nc6 18. h4 Nb4 19. Bxb4 Bxb4 20. e5 Rc8 21. h5 $40) 17. e5!? {Opening the h1-a8 diagonal for White's light-squared bishop.} ({Still, I'm not sure} 17. d5 exd5 18. exd5 Ne5 19. Qc2 Qd6 20. e4 {with the idea of h4 would be part of fun for Black.}) 17... cxd4 {Risky!} (17... Rc8 {looked helpful before Black takes on d4:} 18. Bf3 O-O 19. Rc1 Na5 20. Bxa5 Qxa5 {and I think Black should manage to survive White's attack, since at least one pair of rooks will be exchanged in case of 21.h4 cxd4.}) (17... Qb6!?) 18. Bf3 Rc8 19. Rc1 Qd7? {The losing move.} (19... Qb6 $8 {would probably have saved the day:} 20. Qc2 O-O! 21. exd4 (21. Bxc6? dxe3 22. Be1 Rc7 $19) 21... Nxe5! 22. Qxc8 Nxf3 23. Qc2 Nxd2+ 24. Qxd2 Qd6 $44) 20. Qc2! Na7 21. Qxc8+! Nxc8 22. Bc6 {Now it's piece of cake for the World Champion.} Nb6 23. Bxd7+ Kxd7 24. exd4 Nd5 25. h4! {Opening up the h-file at the cost of a pawn.} Rxh4 26. Rxh4 Bxh4 27. Rh1 Be7 28. Rh7 Bf8 29. Rh8 Ke7 30. Kc2 f6 31. exf6+ gxf6 32. Rh7+ (32. Rh7+ Kd6 33. Ra7 {is hopeless for Black.}) 1-0

