{[%evp 0,40,18,-24,28,15,26,18,26,-23,-24,-24,-33,-33,-11,8,8,-38,-38,-40,-39,-47,-47,-47,-53,-85,-92,-92,-92,-172,-134,-135,-135,-135,-129,-126,-107,-131,-148,-533,-533,-547,-499]} {In this game Magnus proved his real power!} 1. b3 {Bobby Fischer and Bent Larsen favorite side opening repertoire!} g6 2. Bb2 Nf6 3. e4 ({Safer lines are} 3. e3 Bg7 4. Nf3 O-O 5. d4) 3... d6 4. f4 Bg7 5. Nf3 O-O 6. d3 e5! 7. fxe5 Ng4 8. Nbd2 ({Not better alternative was} 8. Nc3 dxe5? (8... Nc6! 9. exd6 cxd6 10. h3 Ne3 11. Qd2 Nb4 12. Rc1 Bh6) 9. h3 Ne3 (9... Nf6 10. Nxe5 Nh5 11. Nf3 Ng3 12. Rg1 Nc6) 10. Qd2 Nxf1 11. Rxf1 Nc6 12. O-O-O a5 13. Kb1 Nd4 14. a4 Bd7 (14... c5!) 15. Qf2 c5 {with great game for Black,Petrosian,T (2663)-Matinian,N (2475) Moscow 2015}) 8... Nc6 9. Qe2 ({Black had strong initiative after} 9. Nc4 f5! 10. exf6 Bxf6 11. d4 Re8 12. Bd3 d5) 9... Ngxe5 10. d4 ({Better was} 10. O-O-O a5) 10... Nxf3+ 11. Nxf3 Re8 12. O-O-O {[#]} Bf5 13. e5 dxe5 (13... Nb4 14. a3 Nxc2 15. g4) 14. Nxe5 ({Black would win a pawn after} 14. dxe5 Qe7 15. Qe3 Nxe5 16. Nxe5 Bxe5 17. Bxe5 Qxe5 18. Qxe5 Rxe5) 14... Nxe5 15. dxe5 Qg5+ 16. Kb1 ({Or} 16. Qd2 Qxd2+ 17. Kxd2 Bh6+ 18. Ke1 Bf4) 16... Bxe5 17. Bxe5 Rxe5 18. Qc4 Rd8 19. Be2 b5! {One more powerful strike of Magnus!} 20. Qxc7 Rc8 0-1

