1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Nf3 O-O 5. Bg5 c5 6. Rc1 cxd4 7. Nxd4 h6 8. Bh4 d5 9. cxd5 g5 10. Bg3 Qxd5 11. e3 Qxa2 12. Qc2 Bxc3+!? $146 {An interesting idea.} ({As far as I know, there is nothing wrong with the main move} 12... Nd5 {except it's a bit easier to play as White:} 13. h4 Nxc3 14. bxc3 (14. hxg5 Na4+ 15. Kd1 Qxb2 16. Qxb2 Nxb2+ 17. Kc2 hxg5 18. Kxb2 Be7 19. Be5 (19. Bd3 Nd7 20. Rh6 Bf6 21. Rc7 Bd8 22. Rc1 Bf6 23. Rc7 Bd8 24. Rc1 {½-½ Nechaeva,M (2410)-Kovanova,B (2369) Yaroslavl 2018}) 19... f6 20. Bg3 Nc6 21. Nxc6 bxc6 22. Rxc6 Rf7 23. Bc4 Bd7 24. Rxe6 Bxe6 25. Bxe6 Kg7 26. Bxf7 Kxf7 $11 {½-½ (38) Brunner,N (2462)-Leko,P (2709) Germany 2017}) 14... Qxc2 15. Rxc2 Be7 16. hxg5 hxg5 17. f4! Nc6 18. fxg5 Bxg5 19. Rh5! f6 (19... Bxe3 20. Nxc6 bxc6 21. Bd6 $36) 20. Nf3 Bxe3 21. Re2 Bc1 22. Re4 e5 23. Bc4+ Kg7 24. Reh4 Kg6 25. Rh7 e4!? (25... Bg4 26. Bd3+ f5 27. Nxe5+ Nxe5 28. Bxe5 Kg5 $8 29. g3 Rg8 30. Rxb7 Rae8 31. Rb5 Rg6 32. Kf2 Rb6 $11 {½-½ (42) Carlsen,M (2882)-Ding Liren (2805) Saint Louis 2019}) 26. Nd2 Ne5 27. R7h6+ Kg7 28. Rh7+ Kg6 29. R4h6+ Kf5 30. Rh5+ Kg6 31. R7h6+ Kg7 32. Rh7+ Kg6 33. R7h6+ Kg7 34. Bxe5 fxe5 35. Rh7+ Kg6 36. R7h6+ Kg7 37. Rh7+ Kg6 38. R7h6+ {½-½ Sevian,S (2654)-Narayanan,S (2611) Douglas 2019}) 13. Qxc3 Ne4 14. Qc2!? (14. Qb4!? {is the first computer choice, but Black is just fine:} Na6 (14... a5!? 15. Qb5 Bd7 16. Qxb7 Nc6! 17. Bd3 (17. Qxd7? Qxb2 $19) 17... Nxg3 18. hxg3 Rab8 19. Qxd7 Ne5 20. Bb1 Qxb2 21. Qc7 Rb7 22. Qc2 Nd3+ 23. Kd2 Nxc1 24. Rxc1 Rc8 25. Qxb2 Rxb2+ 26. Bc2 Ra2 {with an easy draw.}) 15. Bxa6 Qxa6 16. Nb5 (16. Nf3 Nxg3 17. hxg3 e5 18. Qe4 Rd8 19. Nxe5 Qf6 {should be fine for Black}) (16. f3 Nxg3 17. hxg3 e5 18. Ne2 Qe6 $132) 16... b6! 17. O-O (17. Nc7? Qd3! $17) 17... Nxg3 18. fxg3! Qa5 19. Qe4 Ba6 20. Rxf7! Rxf7 21. Qg6+ Kf8 22. Qxh6+ Kg8 23. Qg6+ $11 {A very nice forced draw.}) 14... Qa5+ 15. Ke2 Nxg3+ (15... Nf6 16. h4 {would give White huge compensation, but maybe not enough for an advantage. For example:} g4 (16... Nc6 17. hxg5 Nxd4+ 18. exd4 Qxg5 19. Bh4! {looks dangerous for Black.}) 17. f3 Nc6 18. Nxc6 bxc6 19. Kf2 Rd8 $132) (15... e5 16. Qxe4 exd4 17. Qxd4 Nc6 18. Qc3 $14) (15... f5?! 16. f3 Nxg3+ 17. hxg3 Nc6 18. Nxc6 bxc6 19. Kf2! {is quite ugly for Black.}) 16. hxg3 Kg7 17. f4 {White has a big threat there: b2-b4!} Bd7?! (17... Nc6! {was a much better move, and I believe Black is fine:} 18. Nxc6 (18. Nb3 Qf5 19. Qc3+ e5 $132) 18... bxc6 19. Kf2 (19. b4 Qxb4 20. fxg5 Qg4+ 21. Kf2 Qxg5 $15) 19... Rd8 20. Rd1 Rxd1 21. Qxd1 Qf5 {and Black is definitely not worse.}) (17... gxf4 18. gxf4 {just looks ugly for Black - opening up the g-file.}) 18. b4! {A very nice blow!} Qxb4 (18... Qd8 {would allow the white queen to the a1-h8 diagonal, which looks very dangerous for Black:} 19. Qb2 (19. Nf3!?) (19. b5!?) (19. Qc3!?) 19... Qf6? (19... e5 {is necessary}) 20. fxg5 hxg5 21. Nf5+! $18) 19. fxg5 Rc8? ({It may be that it wasn't too late to play} 19... Nc6 {- some crazy computer line going:} 20. Nf3 (20. gxh6+ Kh8 $132) 20... Rfc8 21. gxh6+ Kh8 22. Qd1 Ne5 23. Rxc8+ Rxc8 24. Nxe5 Qb2+ 25. Kf3 Qxe5 26. Qxd7 Qf6+ 27. Ke2 Qb2+ $11) (19... Rh8 20. Qe4! {looks very dangerous for Black.}) 20. gxh6+ Kh8 21. Qxc8+! Bxc8 22. Rxc8+ Kh7 23. Nf3! {Another brilliant move. Black is completely paralyzed.} (23. Kf2 {would allow} Qd2+ 24. Be2 Nc6! 25. Rxa8 Nxd4 $11) 23... f6 (23... Qb2+ {doesn't help:} 24. Ke1 Qb1+ 25. Kf2 Qb2+ 26. Be2 $18) 24. Kf2 (24. Rc7+ Kh8 25. Nh4 Nd7 26. Ng6+ Kg8 27. h7+ Kg7 28. h8=Q+ Rxh8 29. Rxd7+ Kxg6 30. Rxh8 Qb5+ 31. Rd3 {was winning as well, but the text move is stronger.}) 24... Qb2+ 25. Be2 Na6 {Black has no choice but to sacrfice his a8-rook.} (25... a5 26. Rc7+ Kh8 27. Nh4 $18) 26. Rxa8 Nc5 27. Rd1!? (27. Rh4!?) 27... Ne4+ 28. Kg1! {Again, brilliant!} f5 (28... Qxe2 29. Rd7+ {runs into a forced mate:} Kg6 30. Rg8+ Kh5 31. g4+ Kxh6 32. Rh8+ Kg6 33. Nh4+ Kg5 34. Rg7#) ({So does} 28... Nxg3 29. Rd7+ Kxh6 30. Rh8+ Kg6 31. Nh4+ Kg5 32. Rg7#) 29. Bd3!? Qf2+ (29... Nf2? 30. Rd2 $18) 30. Kh1 Qxe3 31. Bxe4 fxe4 32. Rd7+ {Now it's easy.} Kg6 (32... Kxh6 33. Rh8+ Kg6 34. Rg8+ Kf6 35. Rf8+ Kg6 36. Ne5+ Kg5 37. Rg7+ Kh6 38. Rfg8 $18) 33. Rg8+ 1-0

