1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. g3 Ba6 5. b3 b5 6. cxb5 Bxb5 7. Bg2 d5 8. O-O Nbd7 9. Nc3 Ba6 10. Ne5 {Alternatives seen in practice in this well-known position:} (10. Re1) (10. Bb2) (10. Na4) (10. a3) (10. Rb1) 10... Bd6 (10... Nxe5? 11. dxe5 Nd7 (11... Bb4 12. exf6 Bxc3 13. fxg7 Bxg7 14. Rb1 O-O 15. Ba3 Re8 16. Rc1 $16 {[%csl Ra7,Rc7] B.Avrukh}) 12. Nxd5! exd5 (12... Rc8 13. Nc3 Nxe5 14. Qc2 $16 {1-0 Cernousek,L (2405)-Ftacnik,L (2553)/Slovakia 2008/EXT 2009 (36)}) 13. Qxd5 {[%cal Rd5a8,Re5e6]} Nb6 14. Qc6+ (14. Qa5!?) 14... Qd7 15. Rd1 (15. Bg5!? Be7! 16. Rfd1 Qxc6 17. Bxc6+ Kf8) 15... Qxc6 16. Bxc6+ Ke7 17. Bxa8 Nxa8 18. Bg5+ f6 19. exf6+ gxf6 20. Bf4 $16 {1-0 Kiss,P (2380)-Menacher,M (2334)/Balatonlelle 2005/EXT 2008 (29)}) (10... Bb7?! 11. Bf4 {[%csl Rc7][%cal Ya1c1,Yc3b5] B.Avrukh}) (10... c5 11. Bf4 (11. Bg5 Rc8 12. Nxd7 Qxd7 13. Bxf6 gxf6 14. Rc1 c4 15. e4!? cxb3 16. Qxb3 Bc4 17. Qb2 Bh6 18. Rcd1 Bxf1 19. Bxf1 $44 {1-0 Malakhatko,V (2610)-Cori Tello,D (2262)/Palau 2009/CBM 130 Extra (38)}) 11... Rc8 12. Na4 Nxe5 (12... Bb5 13. Nxc5 Nxc5 14. dxc5 Bxc5 15. b4 Bd6 16. a4 $14 {1-0 Onischuk,A (2653)-Mateo,R (2453)/Mallorca 2004/CBM 104 (102)}) 13. Bxe5 Nd7 14. Bf4 c4 15. Qd2 Be7 16. Rfc1 O-O 17. b4 Bb5 18. Nc5 $14 {1/2 Sriram,J (2431)-Bakre,T (2491)/Visakhapatnam 2004/CBM 103 ext (53)}) 11. Bf4 (11. Nc6!? Qc8 12. a3! {is more energetic:} O-O (12... Qb7 13. Na5 Qb6 14. b4 $16 {B.Avrukh}) (12... Nb8 13. Nb4 Bb7 14. Bb2 O-O 15. Nd3 Nbd7 16. Rc1 Qb8 17. Na4 a5 18. Qc2 $14 {1/2 Lalic,B (2522)-Agrest,E (2563)/Stockholm 2002/CBM 085 ext}) 13. Bg5 (13. Bf4!? Qe8 14. Nb4! Bb7 15. Nd3 $14 {B.Avrukh}) 13... Qe8 (13... Qb7 14. Na5 Qb6 15. b4 h6 16. Bxf6 Nxf6 17. Re1 $16 Rad8? 18. Na4 Qb5 19. e4! $18 {1-0 Perez Rodriguez,L (2391)-Mateo,R (2444)/Havana 2003/CBM 094 ext (27)}) 14. Qd2 Nb6 15. Na5 (15. Nb4! $16 {B.Avrukh}) 15... c5 16. dxc5 Bxc5 17. Bxf6 gxf6 18. Rfc1 $16 {1/2 Beliavsky,A (2665)-Topalov,V (2725)/Madrid 1997/CBM 059/[Avrukh,B] (58)}) {The whole line therefore looks rather dubious for Black.} 11... O-O (11... Bxe5 12. dxe5 Nh5 13. Be3 Nxe5 14. Qd4 Qd6 15. Qa4+ Qc6 16. Qb4 $40 {[%csl Re8]}) 12. Rc1 Bxe5 13. dxe5 Nh5 $146 {[%mdl 8] Improving on the earlier blitz game:} (13... Ng4? 14. Nxd5! exd5 15. Qxd5 {[%cal Rh2h3,Rd5a8]} Nb6 16. Qa5 Bxe2 17. Rfe1 Bd3 18. Red1 (18. h3 $18) 18... Qd4 19. Rd2 Rad8 20. h3 Nxf2 21. Rxf2 Be4 22. Qxa7 Bxg2 23. Kxg2 Qe4+ 24. Kh2 $16 {0-1 Karpov,A (2670)-Carlsen,M (2714)/Moscow 2007/EXT 2008 (92)}) 14. Na4 (14. Be3!? Nxe5 15. Na4 $44 {[%cal Ya4c5]}) 14... Nxf4 15. gxf4 Bb5 16. Nc5 Nxc5 17. Rxc5 c6 18. Qd2 (18. a4 Qb6! 19. Qc2? Bc4) 18... Qb6 19. Rfc1 a5! 20. e4 {White hurries up to create a kingside attack. It turns out that his c5-rook is vulnerable:} (20. a4 Bc4!) 20... a4 {[%csl Gb5] The b5-bishop is now secure.} 21. f5 axb3 22. f6?? {[%mdl 8192]} (22. axb3 Kh8! $14) 22... Qxc5! $19 23. a4 {Desperation.} (23. Rxc5 bxa2 24. Qg5 a1=Q+ 25. Rc1 Qxc1+ 26. Qxc1 h6! {, and Black's material advantage should be sufficient for a win.}) 23... Qxc1+ 24. Qxc1 b2 25. Qxb2 Rxa4 26. Qc1 gxf6 (26... h6!? $19) 27. h4 (27. exf6 Kh8 {[%cal Yf8g8]}) 27... Rfa8 28. Kh2 dxe4 29. exf6 Kh8 30. Qf4 e3 31. Qxe3 Rxh4+ 32. Kg3 Rh5 (32... Rha4 $19) 33. Kg4 Rf5 34. Be4 Rg8+ 35. Kh4 Rxf6?? {[%mdl 8192] Black finally returns the favour.} (35... Rfg5 36. Qxg5 Rxg5 37. Kxg5 c5 38. Bc2 (38. Kh6 Ba4 {[%cal Yc5c4,Yc4c3,Yc3c2]}) (38. Kf4 h5! 39. Kg5 Ba4) 38... Be2 $19 {[%cal Yc5c4,Ye2d3]}) 36. Qc3 Kg7 37. Qg3+ Rg6 38. Qe5+! Rf6 39. Qg5+ Rg6 40. Qe5+ Kf8 {Black can't avoid the perpetual!} (40... f6 41. Qc7+ Kh6 (41... Kh8 42. Bxg6 hxg6 43. Qe7) 42. Qf4+) 41. Qb8+ Ke7 42. Qc7+ Kf6 43. Qf4+ Kg7 1/2-1/2

[Event "Grand Slam Final 4th"]
