1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. Bg5 Bg7 4. Nbd2 h6 5. Bh4 d6 6. e4 g5 7. Bg3 Nh5 8. c3 e6 9. Nc4! {A very strong setup for White.} Nd7 (9... f5 10. Nfd2! {is White's main idea.} Nxg3 11. hxg3 O-O (11... fxe4 12. Qh5+ Ke7 {is critical according to the engine.}) 12. Ne3 d5 13. exf5 exf5 14. Nxd5 (14. Qc2!?) 14... Re8+ 15. Ne3 f4 16. Bc4+ Be6 17. Bxe6+ Rxe6 18. Qb3 Qe8 19. Ne4 Nd7 (19... fxe3? 20. Nc5 $18) (19... Kf8! $132) 20. gxf4 gxf4 21. Ng4 Kh8 22. f3 Rxe4+ 23. fxe4 Qxe4+ 24. Kf2 f3! {As usual MVL finds the best way to mess things up.} 25. gxf3 Rf8 26. Nh2 Qh4+ 27. Kg2 Qg5+ 28. Kf1 Qh5 29. Qc2 c5 30. Qg2 (30. Kg2! $16) 30... cxd4 31. Ng4 Qb5+ 32. Kg1 dxc3 33. bxc3 Qc5+ 34. Qf2 Qxc3 35. Kg2 Ne5 36. Nxe5 Bxe5 37. Rxh6+ Kg7 38. Rhh1 Rf6 39. Rag1 Bd4 40. Kf1+ Kf7 41. Rh7+ Kf8 42. Rh8+ Kf7 43. Rh7+ Kf8 44. Rh8+ {½-½ Naiditsch,A (2701)-Vachier Lagrave,M (2789) Karlsruhe/Baden Baden 2018. A crazy game!}) 10. Nfd2 Nxg3 11. hxg3 b6 12. a4 a6 13. Bd3 Bb7 14. Qe2 Qe7 15. Ne3 {Black's position is awful as he cannot castle either side, and the e3-knight dominates the center.} c5 (15... h5 {was played in the only existing game. Black was ready to sac a full pawn to be able to castle but after} 16. Rxh5 Rxh5 17. Qxh5 O-O-O 18. Qe2 {he had to play} Nb8 {and it is obvious that he has no compensation. 1-0 (37) Ahmadzada,A (2431)-Kovalenko,I (2643) Tornelo 2020}) 16. d5 Nf6 (16... O-O 17. f4 exd5 18. Nf5! Qf6 19. e5! dxe5 20. fxg5 Qxg5 21. Rh5 Qf6 22. Qg4 $18) 17. f4 Qc7 18. O-O-O {Black's position is horrific.} gxf4 19. gxf4 b5 {Desperation.} (19... exd5 20. Nf5!? (20. exd5!?) 20... Kf8 (20... O-O 21. e5 $18) 21. e5! Ne8 22. e6 $18) 20. dxe6 ({There was nothing wrong with} 20. axb5 {but Magnus wanted to checkmate instead!}) 20... fxe6 21. e5 dxe5 22. Bg6+ Kf8 23. f5! b4 (23... exf5 24. Nxf5 $18) 24. fxe6 bxc3 25. Ndc4! {What a domination.} cxb2+ 26. Qxb2 Bc8 27. Qb6 Qxb6 28. Nxb6 Rb8 29. Nxc8 Rxc8 30. Nf5 {A nice picture!} 1-0

