{[%evp 0,53,26,9,128,48,125,113,134,16,129,77,83,51,83,26,96,94,102,39,2,-42,-28,-37,-15,-30,-51,-61,-32,-36,-36,-14,-3,-27,-28,-31,-44,-43,-47,20,-8,-111,-59,19,12,-52,-73,-72,-73,46,262,289,306,332,348,370]} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Nc6 6. a3 Be7 7. f4 O-O!? (7... d6 {is obviously the other option.}) 8. e5 Nd5! (8... Nxd4 9. Qxd4 Ng4 {is also critical for the engine, but after} 10. Be2 Nh6 {it is difficult to believe that Black is totally fine.}) (8... Ne8 9. Nf3 f6 10. Bd3 fxe5 11. fxe5 d6 12. exd6 Nxd6 13. O-O $14 {1-0 (31) Lutikov,A-Khasin,A Moscow 1961}) 9. Nxd5 exd5 10. Nxc6 (10. Nf3 d6 $132 {0-1 (39) Lanc,A (2393)-Pacher,M (2357) SVK 2009}) 10... bxc6 (10... dxc6 {just looks fine and safe for Black - but the game move as well.}) 11. Bd3 Bc5 (11... Qb6! {was probably more precise. Black will play ...d6 next and I can't even find equality for White.}) 12. Qf3 d6 13. Be3 Rb8?! (13... Bxe3! 14. Qxe3 Re8 15. O-O f6 $15) 14. b4 Bxe3 15. Qxe3 a5 (15... Re8 16. O-O f6 {now allws} 17. Qxa7 $13) 16. O-O axb4 17. axb4 dxe5?! (17... Rxb4! 18. Ra8 Qc7 19. exd6 Qxd6 20. Rxc8 Rxc8 21. Qh3 Rcb8 22. Qxh7+ Kf8 23. Qh8+ Ke7 {does not seem to work for White.}) 18. fxe5 Rxb4 19. Ra8! {Suddenly Black should be very careful.} g6? (19... Qb6 20. Qxb6 Rxb6 21. e6 Bxe6 22. Bxh7+ Kxh7 23. Rxf8 {and Black should easly hold a draw.}) 20. e6!! (20. Bf5 gxf5 21. Rxc8 Qxc8 22. Qg5+ {would have been a cute draw.}) 20... fxe6 21. Rxf8+ Qxf8 22. g3! (22. Qe1!? Rb6 23. Qf1 Qe8 24. Ba6 Rxa6 25. Qxa6 Bxa6 26. Rxe8+ Kf7 {should be a draw.}) 22... Rb1+? (22... e5! {was necessary:} 23. Qe1! (23. Qxe5 Rb1+ 24. Kg2 Bh3+ 25. Kxh3 Qxa8 26. Qe6+ $11) 23... Rb6 (23... Rb2 $144 24. Ba6 Qc5+ 25. Kh1 Qxc2 26. Rxc8+ Kf7) 24. Bf1 Rb2 25. Bh3 Qc5+ 26. Kh1 Qxc2 27. Rxc8+ Kf7 28. Qf1+ Qf2 29. Rc7+ Kf8 30. Qxf2+ Rxf2 31. Rxc6 $14) 23. Kg2 e5 24. g4!! (24. Qxe5 Bh3+ 25. Kxh3 Qxa8 26. Qe6+ $11) 24... e4? (24... Rb4 $8 {was the last chance:} 25. h3 (25. Ba6 Rxg4+ 26. Kh1 d4 27. Qe2 Kg7 28. Rxc8 Qf4 $132) 25... Rf4 26. Ba6 Bxa6 27. Rxf8+ Rxf8 28. Qxe5 $16) 25. Ba6 Bxa6 26. Rxf8+ Kxf8 27. Qa3+ {Make a few mistakes against the World Champion, and you'll pay for them, in whatever position!} 1-0

