{[%evp 0,76,39,28,26,18,6,18,25,-21,7,7,-9,-9,14,14,36,4,15,7,24,-2,12,4,34,51,53,8,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,-41,-58,-58,-50,-153,-153,-164,-164,-156,-147,-138,-142,-142,-142,-142,-132,-179,-179,-179,-179,-179,-179,-179,-179,-179,-179,-195,-190,-211,-188,-253,-229,-188,-425,-435,-435,-443,-445,-452,-443] Carlsen finally managed to beat So in a match - unfortunately for both of them it was only the fight between beaten semi-finalists for 3rd place. A concentrated performance brought Magnus a 3:1 lead after day 1. Wesley tried to get back into the fight with a sharp line against the Nimzo, got a promising position... and this is what happened:} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. f3 ({The match situation requires something more enterprising, than Wesley's usual} 4. Qc2) 4... Nc6!? {A rare side-line. We'll check the more usual reactions:} (4... c5 5. d5 O-O (5... b5 6. e4 d6 7. Bd2 Bxc3!? 8. Bxc3 b4 {is one plausible line:} 9. Bd2 O-O 10. Ne2 (10. Be3 exd5 11. cxd5 Nfd7 12. Ne2 f5 13. exf5 ({After} 13. Nf4 {a typical engine line is} Qh4+!? 14. g3 Qf6 15. Ne6 fxe4 16. fxe4 Rf7 {} 17. Ng5 Rf8 18. Bh3 Qxb2 19. Be6+ Kh8 20. Nxh7 Qg2 21. Nxf8 Qxh1+ 22. Kd2 Qxd1+ 23. Rxd1 Nxf8 24. Bxc8 Nbd7 25. Bxd7 Nxd7 26. Bf4 Re8 $11) 13... Rxf5 14. Ng3 Re5 15. Kf2 Qh4 {Aronian,L (2758)-Carlsen,M (2876) Douglas 2019} 16. Bd3!? Rxe3!? 17. Kxe3 Qd4+ 18. Ke2 Ne5 19. Nf5 Qxb2+ 20. Qc2 Nxd3 21. Qxb2 Nxb2 22. Ne7+ Kf8 23. Nxc8 Nc6 24. Nxd6 (24. dxc6 Rxc8 $13) 24... Nd4+ 25. Kd2 Ke7 $44) 10... Nh5 11. Be3 f5 12. dxe6 Bxe6 13. exf5 Rxf5 14. Qd2 Nd7 15. O-O-O (15. Ng3!? Qh4 16. O-O-O (16. Bf2 Re5+ 17. Ne4 Qe7 18. O-O-O d5 19. cxd5 Rxd5 20. Qc2 $13) {forces Black to play accurately:} 16... Nxg3 17. hxg3 Qxh1 18. Bd3 Rh5! (18... Qh2? 19. Bxf5 Bxf5 20. Qd5+ $18) (18... Qh5?! 19. g4 Qf7 20. gxf5 Bxc4 21. Be4 Re8 22. b3 d5 23. bxc4 dxe4 24. Qxd7 exf3 25. Qd3 fxg2 26. Rg1 $16) 19. Be4 (19. Rxh1 Rxh1+ 20. Kc2 Ne5) 19... Re8 20. Rxh1 Rxh1+ 21. Kc2 Bf7 22. Qxd6 (22. Bc6 Bg6+ 23. Kb3 Nb6! 24. Bxe8 Bxe8 25. Kc2 B