{[%evp 0,62,32,-14,-21,-20,-18,-18,-35,-50,-25,-17,-17,-15,6,-3,1,20,0,-22,-22,-6,-21,-26,-15,-52,-74,-58,-65,-94,-83,-84,-81,-116,-103,-114,-110,-140,-115,-114,-110,-233,-215,-273,-288,-286,-294,-323,-251,-260,-334,-361,-367,-370,-417,-436,-415,-449,-460,-457,-468,-460,-458,-628,-700]} 1. c4 Nf6 2. Nc3 e5 3. Nf3 Nc6 4. d4 exd4 5. Nxd4 Bb4 6. g3 Na5!? {New direct approach by great player and trainer IGM Sergey Rublevsky. Giri tried this idea after preliminary exchange} (6... Bxc3+ 7. bxc3 Na5 8. e4 (8. Qd3!) 8... O-O 9. f3 d6 10. h4 ({Why not to complete development} 10. Be2) 10... Be6 11. h5 h6 (11... Bxc4) 12. g4 Nd7 13. g5 hxg5 14. h6 g6 15. h7+ Kh8 16. Qc2 c5 {with big advantage, Nepomniachtchi,I (2784)-Giri,A (2764) chess24.com INT 2020}) ({Not so strong is similar attack} 6... Ne5 7. Qb3 Bc5 (7... c5 8. Nc2 b5!?) 8. Nc2 (8. Be3 Nfg4 9. Bh3) 8... O-O 9. Bg2 d6 10. Na4 Bb6 11. Nxb6 axb6 12. Qc3 Re8 (12... Bf5!? 13. Bxb7 Ra7 14. Bg2 Ne4) 13. O-O d5!? (13... Ra7!? 14. Nd4 Bd7) 14. cxd5 Nxd5 15. Qd4 Nf6 16. Qxd8 Rxd8 17. Bf4 {Bishop pair promise some avantage, Artemiev,V (2701)-Lazavik,D (2544) Sochi RUS 2023}) 7. Qd3!? ({Risky pawn sac was possible} 7. Bg2 Bxc3+ 8. bxc3 Nxc4 9. O-O O-O 10. e4 d6 11. Qe2 Nb6 12. Ba3 (12. Bg5 Re8) 12... Re8 13. Qd3 Nfd7 $17 {Stocek,J (2567)-Rublevsky,S (2683) Plovdiv 2010}) 7... d5 8. cxd5 Qxd5 9. Qb5+ Bd7 10. Qxd5 Nxd5 11. Bd2 Nxc3 12. Nc2 {[#]} ({Black pawn structure is without weaknesses after} 12. bxc3 Be7 13. e4 O-O-O) 12... Nxa2! 13. Nxb4 Nxb4 14. Rxa5 ({Huge problems faced White after} 14. Bxb4 Nb3 15. Ra3 Nd4 16. Kd2 O-O-O 17. Rxa7 Kb8 18. Ra3 Bc6) 14... Nc2+ 15. Kd1 Nd4 16. f3 ({Black kept extra pawn after} 16. Bg2 Bc6 17. Re5+ Kd7) 16... Be6 ({Equally strong was} 16... b6 17. Re5+ Be6 18. Bh3 O-O-O) 17. Bc3 b6 ({Possible was} 17... O-O-O 18. Ke1 a6) 18. Rg5 O-O-O 19. Ke1 g6 20. Kf2 f6 {Black wins exchange and game is over.} 21. Rg4 Bxg4 22. fxg4 Rhe8 23. h4 c5 24. h5 g5 25. h6 Nb5 26. Be1 Rd1 27. e3 Nd6 28. Kf3 Kc7 29. Be2 Rb1 30. Bd3 Rxb2 31. Bxh7 Nc4 0-1

