1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. Nf3 Bg7 5. Bg5 Ne4 6. Bf4 Nxc3 7. bxc3 c6 {A rare, rather passive continuation but in the hands of GM Magnus Carlsen it becomes quite playable!} (7... c5 {and}) (7... O-O {are usually played}) 8. e3 O-O 9. cxd5?! {This move, giving the c6-square back to Black's knight, is rather harmless. Practice has seen other options posing more problems to Black:} (9. Bd3!? dxc4 10. Bxc4 Nd7 11. O-O Nb6 12. Bb3 Nd5 13. Ne5 Nxf4 14. exf4 Qd6 15. Re1 e6 16. Qf3 Re8 17. h4! $40 {1-0 Spassky,B-Byvshev,V/Leningrad 1955/EXT 1999 (30)}) (9. Be2 dxc4 (9... Qa5 10. Qb3 Nd7 11. O-O e5 12. Bg3 dxc4 13. Bxc4 e4 14. Nd2 b5 15. Be2 Nf6 16. a4 $16 {1-0 Malaniuk,V (2615)-Markowski,D (2305)/Koszalin 1997/CBM 059 ext (28)}) (9... Nd7 10. O-O Nb6 11. c5 Nd7 12. c4 dxc4 13. Bxc4 b5 14. Be2 a5 15. Rc1 Nf6 16. Ne5 Bb7 17. Bf3 Nd5 18. Bg3 $14 {1-0 Movsziszian,K (2525)-Kuehn,P (2230)/Hamburg 1994/EXT 1997 (35)}) 10. Bxc4 {- 9.d3}) (9. h3!? Qa5 10. Qb3 Nd7 11. a4 dxc4 12. Bxc4 b5 13. Bd3 Nb6 14. O-O Nxa4 15. c4 a6 16. Rfc1 Ra7 17. Ne5 Bxe5 18. Bxe5 Qd8 19. Qc2 Bd7 20. h4 $40 {1-0 Gabriel,C (2555)-Gauglitz,G (2400)/Germany 1998/GER-chT (27)}) 9... cxd5 10. c4 (10. Bd3 {is safer.}) 10... Nc6 11. c5 Bg4 (11... f6!? {[%cal Ye7e5] , and Black can even fight for the initiative.}) 12. Be2 Bxf3 13. Bxf3 e5 {A classic equalising plan. The position quickly simplifies.} 14. dxe5 Bxe5 15. Bxe5 Nxe5 16. O-O Nxf3+ 17. Qxf3 Rc8 18. Rac1 Qd7 19. Rfd1 Rfd8 20. Qe2 Rc6 21. Qb2 Rdc8 22. Qa3 b6 23. cxb6 Rxc1 24. Rxc1 Rxc1+ 25. Qxc1 axb6 26. Qb2 Qc6 27. h3 h5 28. a4 Qxa4 29. Qxb6 Qa1+ 30. Kh2 Qe5+ 31. Kg1 Qa1+ 32. Kh2 Qe5+ 33. Kg1 1/2-1/2

