1. c4 Nf6 2. Nc3 c5 3. Nf3 e6 4. e4 Nc6 5. Be2 e5 6. d3 d6 7. a3 Be7 8. b4 b6 (8... cxb4 9. axb4 Nxb4 10. O-O O-O 11. Ba3 $44 {is good compensation for White.}) 9. O-O O-O 10. Rb1 Nd4 11. bxc5 bxc5 12. Bg5 Be6 13. Rb7 Nd7 14. Bxe7 Qxe7 15. Qa4 Nb6! {A nicely calculated move.} 16. Qa6 (16. Rxe7 Nxa4 17. Nxa4 Nxe2+ $17) 16... Bc8! 17. Rxe7 Bxa6 18. Rb1?! (18. Nxd4! exd4 19. Nd5 $11 {leads to equality.}) 18... Rfb8 (18... Nxe2+ 19. Nxe2 Rfc8 $17 {with the threat of ...f8 traps the e7-rook.}) 19. Kf1 Kf8 20. Rc7 Ne6 21. Rc6 Rd8?! (21... Ke7 22. Nd5+ Kd7 23. Rcxb6 (23. Nxb6+ Kxc6 $19) 23... axb6 24. Rxb6 Bb7 $19) 22. a4 Bb7 23. Rcxb6 axb6 24. Rxb6 {White has a pawn for the exchange but the position is clearly in Black's favour. Look how carefully Carlsen circumvents all the possible traps and tactics and brings home the full point, ok almost the full point as he agreed to a draw in a clearly better position.} Bc8 25. Bd1 Ra6 26. Rb2 Bd7 27. g3 Bc6 28. Ke1 Rda8 29. Ra2 Rb6 30. Kd2 g6 31. Kc1 Nd4 32. Nd2 Rb4 33. Rb2 Rab8 34. Nb5 Rxb2 35. Kxb2 Ke7 36. Kc3 Bd7 37. f4 f6 38. Nf1 exf4 39. gxf4 Ne6 40. f5 gxf5 41. Ne3 Nf4 42. exf5 Bc6 43. d4 Be4 44. d5 Ng2 45. Nxg2 Bxg2 46. Bc2 Bf3 47. Kb3 Ra8 48. Nc7 Ra7 49. Nb5 Ra8 50. Nc7 Ra7 51. Nb5 {With this win Magnus Carlsen became not only the London Chess Classic winner but also the Grand Chess Tour Champion.} 1/2-1/2

