1. Nf3 d5 2. d4 Nf6 3. c4 e6 4. Nc3 Be7 5. Bg5 h6 6. Bh4 O-O 7. e3 Ne4 8. Bxe7 Qxe7 9. Rc1 c6 10. Be2 Nxc3 11. Rxc3 dxc4 12. Bxc4 Nd7 13. O-O b6 14. Qc2 (14. Bd3 {is more ambitious.}) 14... Bb7 15. Bd3 c5 16. Bh7+ Kh8 17. Be4 Bxe4 18. Qxe4 {For this line - see article by GM P.Lukacs and IM L.Hazai in CBM 142, particularly annotations to Borovikov - Bakre.} Rac8 (18... Nf6 19. Qc2 Nd5 20. Rc4 cxd4 21. Nxd4 Qf6 22. Rc1 Rfd8 23. h3 a6 24. a3 b5 25. Rc6 Ne7 26. Rc7 Nd5 27. Rb7 Ne7 28. Rc7 Nd5 29. Rc6 Ne7 30. Rc5 Ra7 31. Qe4 Rad7 $11 {1/2 Borovikov,V (2601)-Bakre,T (2509)/Kavala GRE 2010/CBM 142/[Lukacs/Hazai] (46)}) (18... f5?! 19. Qf4 Rae8 20. Rd1 e5 21. dxe5 Nxe5 22. Nxe5 Qxe5 23. Qxe5 Rxe5 24. Rd7 f4 25. Rxa7 Rd5 26. h3 Rd1+ 27. Kh2 Rd2 28. exf4 Rxf4 29. Rg3 g5 30. Re3 {1-0 Ponomariov,R (2754)-Miroshnichenko,E (2651)/Kiev 2011/CBM 143 (34)} Kg8! $14) ({Recent practice has seen solid, apparently equalising plans for Black:} 18... Rfe8 19. Rfc1 Kg8 20. h3 e5 21. dxe5 Nxe5 22. Qxe5 Qxe5 23. Nxe5 Rxe5 24. Rd1 Kf8 25. g4 Ke8 {1/2 Malinin,Y (2344)-Krivonosov,O (2448)/Klaipeda 2011/EXT 2012}) (18... cxd4 19. Nxd4 Nc5 20. Qc2 a5 21. Nb3 Nxb3 22. Qxb3 Qb7 23. Rfc1 Rfc8 24. g3 Rxc3 25. Qxc3 Rd8 26. Qc6 Qb8 27. a4 Rd2 28. b3 Rd3 29. Rc3 Rxc3 30. Qxc3 {1/2 Gurevich,M (2617)-Miroshnichenko,E (2651)/Konya 2011/CBM 143 Extra}) {GM Magnus Carlsen finds another, quite simple option. Still, he has to work a while to reach a draw.} 19. Rfc1 (19. Qb7 Qd6!) 19... Rc7 20. Qc2 Rfc8 21. h3 {Too slow.} (21. b4!? Nf6 $140 !? 22. bxc5! Nd5 23. Rc4 b5 24. Rc3 Nxc3 25. Qxc3 $44 {[%csl Gc5]}) 21... Nf6 22. Rc4 Ne8 23. dxc5 Rxc5 24. Qb3 Rxc4 25. Rxc4 Rxc4 26. Qxc4 Nd6 27. Qc6 {Black holds this position with accurate defence.} Kg8 28. Ne5 (28. e4!?) 28... Qd8 29. Nd7 Ne4 30. b3 (30. Qb7 Nc5! 31. Nxc5 Qd1+ 32. Kh2 Qd6+ 33. f4 Qxc5 34. Qb8+ Kh7 35. Qxa7 Kg6 $11) 30... Nf6 31. Ne5 Nd5 32. g3 Qe7 33. h4 g6 34. Kg2 Kg7 35. Nd3 Qd8 36. Qc4 Nf6 37. e4 g5 38. hxg5 hxg5 39. Qc3 Kg8 40. Kf3 Nd7 41. Ke3 Nf6 42. a4 Ng4+ 43. Kf3 Nf6 44. b4 Qd7 45. b5 Qd8 46. Ke3 Ng4+ 47. Ke2 Nf6 48. Qc4 Qa8 49. Ke3 Qd8 50. Kf3 Kg7 51. Qc3 Qh8 52. Qd4 Qh1+ 53. Ke3 Qd1 54. Ne5 Qe1+ 55. Kf3 Qh1+ 56. Ke3 Qe1+ 57. Kf3 Qh1+ 1/2-1/2

