{[%evp 0,90,26,26,29,0,-3,-3,-3,3,41,60,17,82,71,78,97,85,75,75,79,62,94,14,0,-24,21,10,10,48,31,18,16,26,48,9,35,-12,0,-5,-28,-110,-110,-132,-99,-207,-215,-278,-168,-171,-214,-214,-169,-215,-254,-255,-207,-207,-207,-325,-207,-207,-225,-192,-192,-192,-199,-150,-207,-162,-162,-166,-166,-174,-166,-208,-216,-248,-226,-286,-273,-284,-279,-336,-330,-444,-389,-517,-495,-624,-631,-631,-847]} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 d5 4. Nc3 dxc4 5. e4 b5 6. e5 Nd5 7. Nxb5 Nb6 8. a4!? ({On the previous day, Magnus played} 8. a3 {and after} Nc6 9. Be3 Na5 10. Qc2 a6 11. Nc3 Be7 12. Rd1 Bb7 13. Be2 Qd7 14. h4 Bc6 15. Rh3 {White got a slightly better position. However, the World Champion decided to change his 8th move - so he probably didn't like something. It could be that 10...a6 was unprecise. 0-1 (56) Carlsen,M (2863)-Nakamura,H (2736) chess24.com 2020}) (8. Be2 {is the main line. Several games continued} Nc6 9. O-O Be7 10. Qd2! {(trying to get the queen to g4) and White generally got better, e.g.} Qd7 11. Rd1 Bb7 12. Nc3 Nb4 13. Qf4 f5 14. exf6 gxf6 15. b3 cxb3 16. axb3 $16 {1-0 (36) Cheparinov,I (2670)-Moiseenko,A (2635) chess24.com 2020. I must say I have no idea why Nakamura is insisting with this line - I don't like it for Black!}) 8... Qd7 $146 (8... a5 9. Be2 Be7 10. O-O Nc6 11. Be3 Ba6 12. Nd2 O-O 13. Nxc4 $16 {½-½ (24) Fedoseev,V (2678)-Xiong,J (2709) chess.com 2020}) (8... Nc6 9. a5 Ba6 10. Na3 Bb4+ 11. Bd2 c3 12. bxc3 (12. Bxa6!?) 12... Bxf1 13. axb6 Bxg2 14. Rg1 Bxf3 15. Qxf3 Nxd4 16. Qe4 axb6 17. cxb4 Qd5 18. Qxd5 exd5 19. Rg3 $16 {1-0 (41) Tomashevsky,E (2702)-Alekseenko,K (2650) Konya 2019}) 9. Be2 Nc6 10. O-O Na5 11. Ng5 {A typical manoeuvre.} (11. Rb1!? Bb7 12. b4 cxb3 13. Bd2 Nac4 14. Qxb3 Bd5 15. Qd1 $14) 11... h6 (11... Be7 12. Ne4 a6 13. Nc5! Qc6 (13... Bxc5 14. dxc5 axb5 15. cxb6 cxb6 16. axb5 $16) 14. Bf3 Nd5 15. Nc3 $14) (11... Nb3?! 12. d5!! {An amazing move.} a6 (12... Nxa1 13. dxe6 fxe6 14. Nxe6 $16) 13. Nd4 (13. dxe6 fxe6! 14. Qxd7+ Kxd7 15. Rd1+ Nd5 16. Bxc4 Nxa1 17. Nxe6 axb5 18. Bxd5 Rxa4 $13) 13... Nxd4 (13... Nxa1 14. dxe6 fxe6 15. Bf3 Nd5 16. Bg4 $16) 14. Qxd4 h6 15. a5 Nxd5 16. Ne4 Be7 17. Qxc4 $14) (11... Bb7?! 12. Bh5! g6 13. Bf3 $14) 12. Ne4 Bb7 13. Nc5 Bxc5 14. dxc5 Nd5 15. Ra3! a6 (15... O-O 16. Bxh6 gxh6 17. Rg3+ Kh8 18. Qd2 f5 19. exf6 Rxf6 20. Qxa5 $18) 16. Nd4 Ne7 17. Qd2 (17. Rg3!? O-O-O 18. Be3 $14) 17... Qd5 18. Rg3 Qxc5 19. b4?! {The start of a bad idea.} (19. Qf4! Rg8 (19... g6 20. b4 cxb3 21. Nxb3 Nxb3 22. Rxb3 Qd5 23. Rg3 $14) (19... Nd5?! 20. Qh4 $16) (19... O-O-O 20. Be3) 20. b4! cxb3 (20... Qxb4? 21. Bh5 g6 22. Ba3 $16) 21. Nxb3 Nxb3 22. Rxb3 g5 23. Qe3 Qxe3 24. fxe3 Bc6 25. Bh5 Rg7 26. Rc3 $44) (19. Rxg7? O-O-O $17) 19... cxb3 20. Ba3?! (20. Nxb3 Nxb3 21. Rxb3 Qd5 22. Qxd5 Bxd5 23. Rc3 $44) 20... Qxa3 21. Qxa5 Bd5 22. Rxg7 (22. Qc3 Qa2 $17) 22... c5! 23. Bh5 cxd4 {White's attack is just falling.} 24. Rxf7 (24. Bxf7+? Kf8 $19) 24... Kd7 25. Bg4 {Threatening Qxd5+ thanks to a double pin!} Kc6 26. Bxe6 (26. Rf6 Kb7 27. Bxe6 Bxe6 28. Rxe6 Nc6 $19) 26... Bxe6 27. Rf6 Kd7!? (27... Kb7 28. Rxe6 Nc6 $19) 28. Qb6 Bd5 29. Rd6+ Ke8 (29... Kc8!? 30. Qxd4 b2 $19) 30. Rxd5 Nxd5 31. Qc6+ Ke7 32. Qb7+ Ke6 33. Qc6+ Ke7 34. Qb7+ Ke6 35. Qc6+ Kf5 $8 36. Qxd5 Qe7 {White has got a few practical chances, but a rook is a rook.} 37. e6+ Kg6 38. Qe4+ Kg7 39. Qxd4+ Kg8 40. Qg4+ Qg7 41. Qc4 b2 42. f4 Rb8 43. Qe4 Rh7 44. Rb1 Qb7 45. Qe2 Rc7 0-1

