{[%evp 0,55,26,25,30,-9,-9,3,3,-13,15,15,31,1,31,22,39,65,61,63,123,119,113,78,123,99,121,97,135,91,103,86,109,43,170,89,173,187,171,173,173,168,168,195,199,193,224,89,192,136,232,262,222,273,303,297,721,721]} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 d5 4. Nc3 Be7 5. Bf4 O-O 6. a3!? Nbd7 ({The main move here is} 6... b6 {but Nakamura decided otherwise.}) 7. Nb5 Ne8 {By playing this move, Black slows down his play, but of course White is also losing time with his b5-knight.} (7... c6? {loses to} 8. Bc7 Qe8 9. Nd6 $18) 8. e3 dxc4 {Probably not the best move, but Black has been struggling to equalize with other moves as well.} (8... a6 9. Nc3 Nef6 10. cxd5 Nxd5 11. Nxd5 exd5 12. Bd3 c5 13. Rc1 (13. O-O!?) (13. dxc5 Nxc5 14. O-O {is possible as well.}) 13... cxd4?! (13... Qa5+ {looked much more natural, but here Blac can try the interesting} 14. b4!? cxb4 15. Bc7 b6 16. axb4 Qxb4+ 17. Ke2 {with full compensation.}) (13... c4 14. Bb1 Qa5+ {might be best.}) 14. Nxd4 (14. Bc7!?) 14... Qa5+ 15. Kf1 Qd8 16. g4!? Nc5 17. Bb1 Ne4 18. Kg2 Bg5 19. f3 Nd6 20. Re1 $14 {½-½ (67) Mamedyarov,S (2772)-Zvjaginsev,V (2627) Moscow 2019}) (8... Ndf6 9. Rc1 c6 (9... Nh5 10. Bg3 g6 11. Be2 dxc4 12. Bxc4 Nd6 13. Qe2 Bd7 14. O-O a6 15. Nc3 Rc8 16. b4 $14 {1-0 (33) Fressinet,L (2670)-Aleksandrov,A (2601) Rijeka 2010}) 10. Nc3 b6 11. Qa4 Bb7 12. cxd5 exd5 13. Ne5 b5 14. Qc2 $14 {½-½ (36) Vitiugov,N (2709)-Yu Yangyi (2764) Shenzhen 2018}) (8... c6 {was played the most often:} 9. Nc3 f5 10. h3 (10. h4!?) 10... Nd6 11. cxd5 exd5 12. Bd3 Nf6 13. Ne5 {and there were several games, but White is a bit better.}) 9. Bxc4 c5?! $146 {This just seems like a poor (and surely decided over-the-board) novelty. Black had two tries to equalize.} (9... a6 10. Nc3 b5 11. Be2!? (11. Bd3 Bb7 12. b4!? a5 13. Rb1 axb4 14. axb4 Bxf3 15. Qxf3 Ra3 16. Kd2 {was played in the game Sanikidze,T (2527)-Maghalashvili,D (2504) GEO 2015, 0-1 (65), but Black after} Bd6!? $146 {the position is unclear.}) 11... c5 12. O-O Bb7 13. d5 (13. dxc5 Nxc5 14. b4 Ne4 15. Nxe4 Bxe4 {shouldn't promise White anything.}) 13... exd5 14. Nxd5 Bd6 15. a4 c4 (15... Ndf6!?) (15... Nb6!?) 16. Bg5 f6 17. Bh4 Nc5 18. axb5 axb5 19. Nc3 Rxa1 20. Qxa1 Bxf3 (20... Nb3!?) 21. gxf3 Qb8 22. Bg3 Bxg3 23. hxg3 $14 {1-0 (32) Mamedyarov,S (2772)-Jakovenko,D (2698) Jerusalem 2019}) (9... Nd6 10. Qc2!? (10. Nxd6 Bxd6 11. Bxd6 cxd6 12. O-O b6 (12... Nf6!?) 13. Rc1 Bb7 14. d5! e5 15. Bb5 Nf6 (15... Rc8! 16. Bc6?! Ba6 17. Re1 Nc5 $132) 16. Bc6 Qe7 17. Nxe5! dxe5 18. d6 Qe6 19. Bxb7 Rad8 20. Qa4 a5 21. Rfd1 Rxd6 22. Rc6 Rxc6 23. Qxc6 Qb3 24. Rd2 $16 {1-0 (57) Xiong,J (2707)-Tabatabaei,M (2642) Khanty-Mansiysk RUS 2019}) (10. Bd3!? Nxb5 11. Bxb5 a6 12. Bd3 c5 13. Qc2! Qa5+ (13... h6 14. O-O cxd4 15. Bc7 Qe8 16. Nxd4 $14) 14. b4! cxb4 15. O-O! bxa3 16. Bxh7+ Kh8 17. Bd3 Nf6 18. Rfb1 $36) (10. Be2!? {with the same idea is 10.Bd3.}) 10... a6 11. Nxd6 cxd6 12. Bd3 h6 13. O-O Nb6 14. e4 Bd7 15. Qe2 $14 {½-½ (50) Wojtaszek,R (2701)-Neverov,V (2489) Legnica 2013}) 10. dxc5 a6 11. Nbd4 Bxc5 ({After} 11... Nxc5 12. O-O {Black also have difficulties to organize his pieces as} b5? {loses to} 13. Nc6 $18) 12. O-O Qe7 13. Rc1 Bd6 14. Ba2! {Black's postion is even worse than it looks. Black could never manage to play ...b5.} Ndf6 (14... Bxf4 15. exf4 $16) 15. Ne5 Nd7? (15... Nd5 16. Bg3 $16) 16. Ndc6! {A nice tactics!} Qh4 (16... bxc6 17. Nxc6) 17. Bg3 Qg5 18. h4 Qf6 19. Ng4 Qxb2 20. Bxd6 bxc6 (20... Nxd6 21. Ne7+ Kh8 22. Qxd6 Qxa2 23. Nxc8 $18) 21. Rc2 Qb5 22. Bxf8 Nxf8 23. h5?! (23. Qd8 {or 23.Qd4 were stronger according to the engine.}) 23... h6 ({Black could simply take on h5. After} 23... Qxh5 {White should still be winning:} 24. Qd8 (24. Qd4!?) 24... Bb7 25. Qb6 Rb8 26. Qa7 Rd8 27. Qxb7 Qxg4 28. Rxc6 {White is just winning.}) 24. Qf3 Qxh5 {Now it's too late!} 25. Qxc6 Nc7 26. Qf3 Nd5 27. e4 e5 28. Nxh6+! 1-0

