1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. Nxd4 Bc5 5. Nxc6 Qf6 6. Qf3 {An interesting line, willing to play an endgam with a slightly better structure.} dxc6 7. Nc3 Be6 8. Be3 Bb4 ({Mostly Black went} 8... Qxf3 9. gxf3 Bxe3 10. fxe3 {and White has a symbolic advantage, though here Black can play 10...Nf6, 10...Ne7, 10...0-0-0, which are all playable.}) ({Blac can also try to keep queens, but he will stand slightly worse:} 8... Qe7 9. O-O-O (9. Bxc5!? Qxc5 10. O-O-O Nf6 11. h3 O-O 12. Kb1 b5 13. Bd3 $36 {1-0 (34) Savchenko,B (2583)-Mamedyarov,S (2752) Moscow RUS 2007}) 9... Nf6 10. h3 Nd7 11. Qg3 O-O-O 12. Qxg7 Bxe3+ 13. fxe3 $14 {1-0 (49) Sulskis,S (2503)-Kantans,T (2510) Tallinn 2018}) 9. O-O-O! (9. Bd2 O-O-O 10. O-O-O (10. a3 Bc5 11. Bd3 Qxf3 12. gxf3 Bd4 13. f4 f5 14. exf5 Bd7 15. Be3 Bxc3+ 16. bxc3 Nh6 17. f6 gxf6 18. Bxa7 Bf5 $44 {½-½ (60) Jones,G (2667)-Howell,D (2644) London 2016}) 10... Qg6 11. Qg3 f5 12. Bd3 Nf6 $13 {0-1 (73) Yu Yangyi (2738)-Nakamura,H (2785) Gibraltar 2017}) 9... Qxf3 $146 (9... Qe7 10. Bd4 Nf6 11. Be2 Bc5 12. Bxc5 Qxc5 13. Qg3 O-O 14. f4 $14 {0-1 (49) Chigaev,M (2616)-Chen,Q (2432) Gibraltar 2020}) (9... Bxc3 10. bxc3 Qxc3 11. Bd4 Qxf3 12. gxf3 f6 13. f4 {would give White very pleasant compensation.}) 10. gxf3 Ne7 11. h4 Bxc3 {Not sure that's a good choice for Black, although anyway White is a bit better.} (11... f6 12. h5 Kf7 13. f4 f5 14. f3 $36) 12. bxc3 Rd8 13. Rxd8+ Kxd8 14. h5 f5 15. c4 Rf8 16. Rg1 Rf7 17. a4 a6 18. a5?! ({After} 18. c5 {or 18.Kb2 White would be clearly better.}) 18... g6 (18... c5! 19. Bxc5 Nc6 $132) 19. Rg5 Rf6 20. hxg6 (20. Bd4 Rf7 21. Kd2 $16) 20... Rxg6 21. c5 Ke8 22. Bd3 Rxg5 (22... Kf7? 23. Rh5 $16) 23. Bxg5 h5 24. Kd2 Kf8?! (24... Ng6!? 25. exf5 Ne5 26. Be4 Bd5 (26... Bxf5 27. Bxf5 Nxf3+ 28. Ke3 Nxg5 29. Bc8 h4 30. Bxb7 h3 31. Bxc6+ {and White should be winning}) 27. Ke3 Nc4+ 28. Kd4 Nxa5 {with some chances for Black.}) 25. Ke3 Kf7 26. Bxe7! {Excellent assessment by the World Champion!} (26. Bf4 {was good as well, but would allow some counterplay with} h4 27. Bxc7 Kf6 $132) 26... Kxe7 27. e5 h4 (27... f4+?! {doesn't work:} 28. Kxf4 h4 29. Bf1 Kf7 30. Kg5! h3 31. Kh4 h2 32. Bg2 $18) 28. f4 Kd7 29. f3 b6 (29... Ke7 30. Kf2 Kf7 31. Kg2 Kg6 32. Kh3 Kh5 33. c3 $22 Kg6! (33... Bd7 34. Bc4 $18) 34. Kxh4 Kh6 {and White will bring his king to d4, play Bc4, and should be winning.}) 30. axb6 cxb6 31. Bxa6!! (31. cxb6 h3 32. Kf2 a5 $132) 31... b5 (31... bxc5 {shouldn't hold a draw, for example:} 32. Be2 Ke7 33. Kf2 Kf7 34. Kg2 Kg6 35. Kh3 Kh5 36. Ba6 c4 37. c3 Bd5 38. Bc8 Kg6 39. Kxh4 Bxf3 40. Be6 Be2 41. Bd7 Bf3 42. Be8+ Kg7 43. Kg5 $18) 32. Kf2 Kc7 33. Kg2 Kb8 34. Kh3 Ka7 35. Kxh4 Kxa6 36. Kg5 {And it is just an easy win for White.} Kb7 (36... Ka5 37. Kf6 Bc8 38. e6 Kb4 39. Kxf5 Kc3 40. Ke5 Kxc2 41. f5 b4 42. e7 Bd7 43. f6 Be8 44. Ke6 b3 45. f7 Bxf7+ 46. Kxf7 b2 47. e8=Q b1=Q 48. Qe4+ $18) 37. Kf6 Bd5 38. c3!? {Not necessary - but putting the pawn on a dark-square when Black has a light-square bishop doesn't hurt.} (38. e6 Kc7 39. Kxf5 $18) 38... Kc7 39. Kxf5 Kd7 40. Kf6 Bxf3 41. e6+ Ke8 42. Ke5 Bg4 43. f5 Bh3 44. f6 Bg4 45. Kd6 Bh3 46. e7! (46. f7+?? Kf8 $11) 46... Kf7 47. Kxc6 1-0

