{[%evp 0,61,26,11,17,5,0,-2,13,7,13,14,15,11,12,-9,5,-9,-1,-54,-19,-43,-31,-38,-8,-9,0,2,15,-3,-11,-16,40,-29,22,-3,31,26,44,7,19,62,28,45,41,41,47,79,0,14,224,224,176,167,308,-106,90,90,90,99,666,666,882,912]} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nf6 4. d3 Bc5 5. Bxc6 dxc6 6. Nbd2 O-O 7. h3 Nd7 8. Nc4 a5 9. g4!? $146 ({More aggressive than} 9. Be3 {which had been played earlier (on the same day!) between the same two players:} f6 10. O-O b5 11. Ncd2 Bxe3 12. fxe3 a4 13. Nh4 c5 14. Nf5 Nb6 $11 {0-1 (43) Nakamura,H (2736)-Carlsen,M (2863) chess24.com 2020}) ({Of course} 9. Ncxe5? {is bad due to} Nxe5 10. Nxe5 Qd4 $17) 9... Re8 10. Rg1 a4 11. Ne3 Bxe3 (11... Nf8 12. Nf5 Ne6 {was the alternative - but apparently Magnus considered it better to avoid a white knight on f5.}) 12. Bxe3 Nf8 13. h4 Qd6 14. Qd2 c5 15. h5 b5 16. Nh4 Qc6 17. Nf5 c4?! {Weakening the dark squares too much.} (17... Ne6 {was the normal move.}) 18. Qb4! {Threatening e7+.} a3 19. b3! cxd3 20. cxd3 Qc2 (20... Qd7 21. O-O-O $16) 21. h6! g6 22. Rc1! Qxd3 23. Rd1?! (23. Ne7+! Kh8 24. Bg5 Ra6 25. Rg3 Qd4 26. Qxd4 exd4 27. Rxc7 $18) 23... Qc2 24. Ng7 Bb7 (24... Bd7! 25. Nxe8 Bxe8 {wouldn't be so clear.}) 25. Nxe8 Rxe8 26. f3 Qxa2 27. Rd2?! {Not the most precise move.} (27. Qxb5 $18) 27... Qb1+ 28. Kf2 a2 29. Qc3 Ra8 (29... f6 30. Rxb1 axb1=Q 31. Qxc7 $18) 30. Rxb1! ({Of course not} 30. Qxe5?? Qxg1+ 31. Kxg1 a1=Q+ $19) 30... axb1=Q 31. Qxe5 (31. Qxe5 Ne6 32. Bd4 Kf8 33. Qh8+ Ke7 34. Bf6#) 1-0

