{[%evp 0,43,26,26,56,38,10,8,19,13,13,5,11,14,17,-3,9,-3,25,15,16,16,18,-5,-14,-14,106,147,179,122,157,192,360,257,483,229,227,252,252,276,281,281,416,388,478,579]} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nf6 4. d3 Bc5 5. Bxc6 dxc6 6. Nbd2 O-O 7. Qe2 Re8 8. Nc4 Nd7 9. Bd2 b5 10. Ne3 Nf8!? {One of the many possible moves, together with 10...Nb6, 10...a5, 10...Bd6.} 11. h4!? (11. Nf5?! {When White plays this move he should be able to take back with his g-pawn.} Bxf5 12. exf5 Qd7 13. Qe4 h6 14. f6? Nh7! 15. fxg7 f5 16. Qe2 e4 $19 {0-1 (34) Oparin,G (2626)-Jakovenko,D (2714) Russia 2016}) 11... Ne6?! $146 (11... a5 12. h5 h6 13. g4! (13. Nf5?! Bxf5 14. exf5 Nd7 15. g4 e4 $19) 13... Bxe3 14. Qxe3 f6 (14... Bxg4 15. Rg1 $44) 15. Nh4 Ne6 $13) 12. Nxe5! {Just a blunder by the World Champion.} a5 (12... Nd4?! 13. Nxf7! {is surely what Black missed.}) (12... Nf4 13. Qf3 $16) 13. Qh5 g6 (13... Qf6 14. N3g4 $16) 14. Qf3 f6 15. Nxc6 Qd7 16. Qxf6 ({The most precise move order would have been} 16. Ng4 Qxc6 17. Qxf6! $18) 16... Qxc6 17. Bc3 {Not the most precise move.} (17. Ng4! Bf8 18. Ne5 {was simple and strong.}) 17... Rf8 18. Qh8+ Kf7 19. Qxh7+ Ke8 20. Qxg6+ Kd7 21. d4 b4 22. dxc5 {Carlsen's blunder on move 11 was just unrecoverable.} (22. dxc5 bxc3 23. O-O-O+ Ke7 24. Nd5+ $18) 1-0

