1. Nf3 d5 2. d4 Nf6 3. c4 c6 4. Nc3 a6 5. a4 e6 6. Bf4 {By far not the main line. There are three more popular continuations:} (6. Bg5 {Bu Xiangzhi (2714)-Movsesian,S (2732)/Nanjing 2008/CBM 128/[Rogozenco] (1-0, 62)}) (6. e3 {Inkiov,V (2495)-Gurevich,M (2634)/Utrecht 2005/CBM 106 ext/[Gutman] (1-0, 32)}) (6. g3 dxc4 (6... Bb4 {Wells,P (2489)-Houska,J (2418)/Sheffield 2011/CBM 143 Extra/[Martin,A] (1/2, 36)}) 7. Bg2 c5 8. O-O (8. dxc5 {Moiseenko,A (2679)-Postny,E (2612)/Mulhouse 2011/CBM 142 Extra/[Postny] (1/2, 80)}) 8... cxd4 9. Nxd4 Bc5 {Mamedyarov,S (2763)-Gashimov,V (2734)/Astrakhan 2010/CBM 137/[Postny] (1/2, 43)}) 6... Be7 {A rare continuation. It is worth mentioning that Carlsen had played this line with White.} (6... c5 7. e3 Nc6 8. Be2 dxc4 9. Bxc4 cxd4 10. exd4 Be7 11. O-O O-O 12. Re1 Nb4 13. Ne5 Bd7 14. d5 exd5 15. Nxd5 Nbxd5 16. Bxd5 Bg4 17. Nxg4 Nxd5 18. Nh6+ Kh8 19. Nf5 Nxf4 20. Rxe7 g6 21. Qxd8 Raxd8 22. Ne3 $14 {Carlsen,M (2786)-Movsesian,S (2732)/Kallithea 2008/CBM 127/[Krasenkow] (0-1, 76)}) (6... a5 7. e3 Na6 8. Be2 Be7 9. O-O Nb4 {Carlsen,M (2775)-Kamsky,G (2723)/Moscow 2008/CBM 126 Extra (1/2, 94)}) 7. e3 Nh5 $146 {The move is new, but the idea is typical in the 5.f4 Queen's Gambit.} (7... O-O) 8. Bd3 Nxf4 9. exf4 a5 10. O-O Na6 11. Rc1 Nb4 12. b3 O-O 13. Bb1 Bf6 14. Re1 b6 15. cxd5 cxd5 16. Na2 Nxa2 17. Bxa2 Ba6 18. Bb1 g6 19. Bd3 Bxd3 20. Qxd3 Rc8 21. g3 1/2-1/2

