6 24. e5 fxe5 25. Bxe5 Nf7 26. Bxg6 Nxe5 27. Bf5 Ng6 28. Bxc8 Nxf4 29. Bxb7 Bxh6 $11 {1/2 Lputian Smbat G (2540)-Romanishin Oleg M (2555)/Lvov 1987 (31)}) 13... cxd4 14. cxd4 Qd6 (14... e6 15. Bh6 Qh4!? 16. Bxg7 Kxg7 17. Qe3 (17. d5 Ne5 18. Qd4 Qf6 19. Bb3 exd5 20. Rxc8 Rxc8 21. exd5 Ba6 22. Nc3 Nd7 23. Ne4 Qxd4 24. Rxd4 Rc1+ 25. Rd1 Rxd1+ 26. Bxd1 Bc4 $17 {0-1 Enchev,I (2435)-Grigorov,G (2497)/Albena BUL 2011/The Week in Chess 867 (33)}) 17... Rfd8 18. Bb5 Qf6 19. Bxc6 Rxc6 20. Rxc6 Bxc6 $11 21. d5?! exd5 22. e5 Qe7 23. Nd4 Bd7 24. f4 Rc8 {0-1 Meyer,M (2348)-Petr,M (2468)/Munich GER 2010/The Week in Chess 840 (52)}) 15. d5 (15. Bf4 {1-0 Zhukova,N (2499)-Nebolsina,V (2310)/Moscow 2010/CBM 138 Extra (39)} e5 $11) (15. Bh6 Qb4! 16. Qxb4 Nxb4 17. Bxg7 Kxg7 18. a3 Nc6 19. d5 Ne5 20. Bb5 Rxc1 21. Rxc1 Rc8 22. Rxc8 Bxc8 23. Nd4 g5 24. f3 {1/2 Stella,A (2310)-Codenotti,M (2169)/Bratto 2010/CBM 138 Extra}) (15. e5!? Qd7 16. e6!? fxe6 17. Nf4 {1-0 Noori,A (2135)-Aghamohammadi,M/Iran 2000/EXT 2003 (28)} Nd8 $13 {A.Giri}) 15... Na5 16. Bb5 Rxc1 17. Rxc1 Rc8 (17... e6! 18. Bf4 Be5 19. Bxe5 Qxe5 20. Nc3 Rc8! $132 {A.Giri}) (17... f5!? {A.Giri}) 18. h3 (18. Rxc8+ Bxc8 19. Nd4! $14 {A.Giri}) 18... Rxc1+ 19. Qxc1 e6 20. Nf4 exd5 21. Nxd5 f5 22. f3 fxe4 23. fxe4 Qe5 $11 {1/2 Topalov,V (2805)-Anand,V (2787)/Sofia 2010/CBM 136/[Giri,Anish] (60)}) 11... Qc7 {A typical idea. After cxb6 axb6 White's queenside pawn majority will be nearly useless.} (11... Ne5 12. Qxd8 Rxd8 13. Bd5 Rb8 (13... Ba6 $142) 14. c6 $16 {1-0 Kanep,M (2523)-Novik,M (2468)/Finland 2008/EXT 2009 (26)}) 12. f4 $146 {This move doesn't look dangerous before Black has played ...e7-e6.} (12. cxb6 axb6 13. Rb1 Rb8 14. Bb5 Ne5 15. f4 Ng4 16. Qc1 Bb7 17. h3 Nxe3 18. Qxe3 Rfc8 19. e5 Bd5 20. c4 Ba8 21. Nc3 Qb7 22. Qe2 e6 23. Rbd1 Rd8 24. Ba4 Rbc8 $44 {0-1 Ju,W (2500)-Gao Rui (2464)/Hefei 2010/CBM 136 Extra (38)}) (12. Qd2?! Rd8 13. Qb2 bxc5 14. Qa3 Ne5 15. Bd5 Rb8 16. Qxc5 Qxc5 17. Bxc5 Ba6 18. c4 e6 $19 {1/2 Zhukova,N (2499)-Nebolsina,V (2310)/Moscow 2010/CBM 138 Extra (54)}) (12. Nd4 Ne5 (12... Bb7 13. cxb6 axb6 14. Nb5 Qe5 15. Bd5 e6 16. Bd4 Qf4 17. g3 Qh6 18. Bxc6 Bxc6 19. Qe2 $16 {1-0 Christiansen,L (2485)-Jansa,V (2480)/Luzern 1982/EXT 1997 (40)}) 13. Nb5 (13. Be2 Bb7 14. cxb6 axb6 15. Nb5 Qc6 16. f3 Nc4?! (16... Rfc8 17. Qb3 Nd7 {[%cal Yd7c5,Yc5a4] R.Simic}) 17. Bxc4 Qxc4 18. Qb3 $14 {1-0 Portisch,L (2635)-Ftacnik,L (2545)/Wijk aan Zee 1985/MCL (72)}) 13... Qb8 14. Be2 (14. Bf4 bxc5 15. Rb1 a6 16. Nd4 Qd6 17. Bd5 Ra7 18. Nc6 Rc7 19. Na5 Rd7 20. Nc4 Qc7 21. Nb6 Rd6 $13 {0-1 Paunovic,D (2320)-Jansa,V (2440)/Vrnjacka Banja 1983/MCD (83)}) 14... bxc5 15. f4 Ng4 16. Bxc5 a6 17. Na3 Qc7 18. Bd4 e5 19. fxe5 Nxe5 $44 {1/2 Aronian,L (2808)-Grischuk,A (2747)/Kazan 2011/CBM 143/[Caruana] (70)}) 12... bxc5 13. Rb1 Rd8 (13... Bg4?! 14. h3 Bxe2 15. Qxe2 Bxc3 16. f5 $44) 14. Qa4 (14. Qe1 Bb7 {[%cal Rc6a5]} 15. Rb5 Na5 16. Rxc5 Qb6 17. Bxf7+!? Kxf7 18. Rf5+ gxf5 19. Bxb6 axb6 $13) (14. Qc2!?) 14... Na5 15. Bd5 Bd7! 16. Qa3 Rac8 17. f5 e6! 18. Bf4 Be5 19. fxe6 fxe6 20. Bb3 Nxb3 21. axb3 Rf8 {Black has comfortably consolidated his position and has no problems.} 22. Qc1 (22. Bxe5 Qxe5 23. Qxa7 Bc6 $44) 22... c4 23. b4 Qb6+ 24. Kh1 Bg7 25. e5 (25. Ra1 $142 $132) 25... Bc6 26. Nd4 Bd5 {[%csl Gd5]} 27. Ra1 Qb7 28. Qc2 Rc7 29. Bg3 Rcf7 30. Rxf7 Qxf7 31. Qe2 g5 32. h3 h5 33. Kg1 h4 34. Bh2 Qg6 35. Rd1 $11 g4!? {[%mdl 512] Black is playing for a win but it is a double-edged sacrifice.} 36. hxg4 Qg5 {[%cal Yg7h6]} 37. Nf5! exf5?! (37... h3! {was correct. White had to find the best defense} 38. Rd4! {[%cal Rh2f4]} (38. gxh3?? Rxf5) {with a logical draw after} 38... Qc1+ 39. Rd1 Qg5 $11) 38. Rxd5 fxg4 39. Kh1 h3 40. gxh3 gxh3 41. Rd4?! (41. Rd1 $142 ! {[%cal Yd1g1,Ye2e4] , and White seizes the initiative.}) 41... Qc1+ 42. Rd1 Qxc3 43. e6 Qb2! 44. Qe4 Qg2+ 45. Qxg2 hxg2+ 46. Kxg2 Re8 47. Rd6 Bf8 48. Rc6 Bxb4 49. Rxc4 a5 50. Rc6 Kg7 51. Kf3 Kf6 52. Ke4 Rxe6+ 53. Be5+ Kf7 1/2-1/2

