{[%evp 0,26,22,22,18,12,12,12,12,-13,-13,1,-2,0,16,11,19,34,45,33,57,53,61,53,55,57,78,53,74]} {Magsodloo promised to become really top Worls player few years ago ,but it seems that he slowed down. But in this game World Champion was in troubles!} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 d5 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Bg5 c6 6. e3 h6 7. Bh4 Be7 8. Bd3 O-O 9. Nge2 Ne8!? {Telling honestly, this Carlsbad system is not easy to handle with Black.So,Magnus wants to create some nonclassical set ups.} 10. Bg3 Nd6 11. O-O Re8 12. Qc2 Bf8 13. Rae1!? $146 {New and interesting. .} ({Magnus had this position on the board.} 13. Bf4 Be6 14. f3 Nd7 15. Rad1 b5 16. e4 Rc8 17. e5 Nc4 18. b3 Ncb6 19. Qd2 {½-½ (70) Grischuk,A (2764)-Carlsen,M (2856) Warsaw 2021}) 13... a5 14. Nf4 {Novelty of Iranian Grandmaster.It was tried a bit different Knight transfer} (14. Nc1 Na6 15. a3 Be6 16. Nb3 Nc4 17. Ne2 a4 18. Bxc4 dxc4 19. Nd2 b5 20. e4 b4 21. Nxc4 Bxc4 22. Qxc4 Rxe4 {with tough game, Bogner,S (2573)-Fressinet,L (2630) Germany 2022}) 14... Na6 15. a3 Qf6? {Overoptimistic.Preferable was to transfer Knight to e6.} (15... Nc7) 16. f3 ({It was unexpected central strike here} 16. e4!? Qxd4 (16... dxe4 17. Nxe4 Nxe4 18. Bxe4 Bd7 19. Re3 Nc7 20. Rf3) 17. exd5 Bd7 18. Rd1 Qb6 19. dxc6 Qxc6 20. Nfd5 Nc5 {and Black holds the position.}) 16... b5 17. Bf2 ({It was possible to prepare programm e3-e4 a bit differently.} 17. Qf2) 17... Nc4 18. g3 ({If White protects Knight differently,then Black equalise after} 18. Qc1 Nc7 19. a4 b4 20. Ne4 Qd8 21. Nd2 Nxd2 22. Qxd2 Ne6) 18... Qd8?! ({Better was to bring Knight to the center} 18... Nc7 19. e4 Ne6) 19. e4 b4 {[#]} ({Magbus did not want to give up the center} 19... dxe4 20. fxe4 Nc7 21. e5 Ne6 22. Rd1 Nxf4 23. gxf4 Bg4 24. Rc1 {and Black still face problems, due to White powerful center.}) 20. exd5! Rxe1 21. Rxe1 Nd6?! ({Better would be} 21... Nb6 {after what White can hold the initiative ,sacrificing a piece} 22. dxc6 bxc3 23. bxc3 Bxa3 24. Qb3 Bd6 25. Bg6! Ra7 26. Bb1) 22. Na4 cxd5 23. Nxd5 Rb8 ({Strong pressure keeps White after} 23... Bb7 24. Ndb6 Rb8 25. d5) 24. Nc5 ({There were two other promising optios here} 24. Nf4) ({and} 24. Re5) 24... Nb5 25. Bxb5? Rxb5 26. Qc4 ({White could keep extra pawn with} 26. Nf4 {but Blacks Bishop pair would be some compensation for it.}) 26... Rb8 27. a4 ({Magnus would keep compensation even after better} 27. Rd1 bxa3 (27... Nxc5 28. dxc5 Be6 29. Qe2! bxa3 30. bxa3 Qc8 31. Nb6 Qc7 32. Qe3 Rd8) 28. bxa3 Qd6) 27... Nxc5 28. dxc5 Bb7 {Now starts forced variation ,where Magnus defends easily.} 29. c6 Rc8 30. Bb6 Qd6 31. Bc7 Qc5+ ({Similar development would follow after} 31... Qxc6 32. Qxc6 Bxc6 33. Ne7+ Bxe7 34. Rxe7 Bxa4) 32. Qxc5 Bxc5+ 33. Kg2 Bxc6 34. Rc1 Bxd5 35. Rxc5 Bb3 36. Bb6 Rxc5 37. Bxc5 Bxa4 38. Bb6 Bc6 39. Bxa5 b3 1/2-1/2

