1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Qc2 O-O 5. Nf3 b6 6. e4 c5?! {A second-rate move.} (6... d5 {and}) (6... Bb7 {are more common continuations.}) 7. e5 (7. dxc5 Bxc5 (7... Bxc3+!? 8. bxc3 e5) 8. e5 Ng4 9. Qe4?! {leads to big complications, quite satisfactory for Black:} (9. Bd3 $142 Nc6! $13) 9... Nxf2 10. Qxa8 Nc6 11. Rg1 Qe7 {[%cal Rc8a6]} 12. Bg5 f6 13. exf6 gxf6 14. Bh4 Ng4 15. h3 {0-1 Toth,B (2405)-Olafsson,H (2370)/Thessaloniki 1984/EXT 1997 (36)} Bxg1 16. hxg4 Be3 $17) (7. a3 {is not dangerous either:} Bxc3+! (7... cxd4 8. axb4 dxc3 9. e5 $36) (7... Ba5 8. e5) 8. bxc3 Bb7 9. Bd3 d5 10. cxd5 exd5 11. e5 Ne4 {, and Black is more or less OK}) 7... Ne8 (7... cxd4 8. a3! (8. Nxd4 Ne8 9. Bd3 (9. Qe4 Nc6 10. Nxc6 dxc6 11. Bd3 f5 12. exf6 Nxf6 13. Qe2 e5 $132 {1/2 Kouatly,B (2460)-Miralles,G (2365)/Montpellier 1985/EXT 1999 (35)}) 9... f5 10. exf6 Nxf6 11. Bg5 (11. O-O Bb7 12. Bg5 h6 13. Bh4 Nc6 14. Nxc6 Bxc6 15. Rad1 Rc8 {1/2 Brglez,R (2285)-Horvath,S (2320)/Austria 1995/EXT 1998 (25)} 16. a3 Be7 17. Bg3 $14 {/=}) 11... h6 12. Bh4 Bb7 13. O-O-O {1-0 Gausel,E (2490)-Bern,I (2360)/Gausdal 1995/EXT 1998 (62)} Qc8 14. Kb1 $14) 8... Bxc3+ $142 (8... dxc3 9. axb4 cxb2 (9... Ne8 10. Qxc3 (10. Bd3!) 10... f6 11. Be2 Bb7 12. O-O fxe5 13. Nxe5 d6 14. Nf3 Qf6 15. Qxf6 gxf6 16. Nd4 $16 Nc7 17. Bh6 Re8 18. Ra3 Kh8 19. Rfa1 Rg8 20. f3 a6 21. b5 a5 22. b4 axb4 23. Rxa8 Bxa8 24. Ra7 Rc8 25. Bg7+ Kg8 26. Bxf6 Kf7 27. Bg5 e5 28. Nf5 {1-0 Erdos,V (2597)-Bruedigam,M (2317)/Deizisau 2011/CBM 141 Extra}) 10. Bxb2 Ne8 11. Bd3 f5 12. exf6 Nxf6 13. Ng5 (13. b5!? {[%csl Ra8,Rb8]} Bb7 14. Ng5) 13... h6 14. Nh7 Nc6! (14... Nxh7 15. Bxh7+ Kh8 16. Bxg7+! Kxg7 17. Qg6+ Kh8 18. Qxh6 Rf6 19. Bg6+ Kg8 20. Ra3 $18) 15. Nxf8 Nxb4 16. Qd2 Qxf8 17. O-O Bb7 18. Ba3 a5 19. Bxb4 axb4 20. Rxa8 Qxa8 21. f3 $16 {1-0 Sakalauskas,V (2437)-Sulskis,S (2570)/Vilnius 2004/CBM 100 ext (62)}) 9. bxc3 Ne8 10. Bd3 (10. cxd4!? Bb7 11. Be2 $14) 10... h6 11. Bh7+ (11. a4!?) 11... Kh8 12. Be4 Nc6 13. cxd4 Bb7 14. Be3 d6 $132 {1/2 Corke,A (2216)-Pokorna,R (2338)/Rijeka 2006/CBM 111 ext (58)}) 8. d5 (8. Bg5 f6 9. exf6 Nxf6 10. dxc5 {1-0 Tomaszewski,R (2405)-Szymczak,Z (2335)/Gdynia 1985/EXT 2001 (41)} Bxc3+! 11. bxc3 Bb7 12. Bd3 h6 $44) (8. Bd3 {may be the most accurate:} f5 (8... h6!?) 9. Bg5 (9. exf6 Nxf6 10. O-O cxd4 11. Ne4 h6 12. Nxd4 Na6 13. a3 Be7 14. b4 Bb7 15. Bb2 Nc7 16. Rfe1 $14 {1/2 Panno,O (2485)-Galliamova,A (2400)/Aruba 1992/CBM 033 (49)}) (9. d5!?) 9... Qc7 10. d5 d6 11. O-O-O (11. O-O $142 $16) 11... Bxc3 (11... dxe5 $142 12. Nb5 Qb7 13. Nxe5 a6 14. Nc3 b5) 12. Qxc3 exd5 13. cxd5 $16 {1-0 Vera Gonzalez Quevedo,R (2535)-Aleksic,N (2445)/Porto San Giorgio 1998/EXT 2000 (23)}) 8... exd5 9. cxd5 d6 10. Bg5 (10. Bd3!? dxe5 11. Bxh7+ Kh8 12. Bd3 Nd6 13. O-O $14 {[%csl Rh8]}) 10... f6 11. exf6 Nxf6 12. O-O-O!? (12. Be2 $14 {[%cal Ye1g1]}) 12... Bxc3 13. bxc3 Bg4 {Black has survived the most difficult times and obtained a decent position. However, he now once again plays inaccurately.} (13... Na6 $142 {[%cal Ya6c7] to cover the e6-square.}) 14. Re1 Bxf3 (14... Nbd7 15. Nh4! Bh5 16. Nf5 Bg6 17. Ne7+ Qxe7 18. Rxe7 Bxc2 19. Kxc2 Rae8 20. Re6! Ne4 21. Be3 $14) 15. gxf3 Nbd7 16. Bd3 h6 17. Bf4 c4! {Black correctly looks for queenside counterplay but has he got enough time?} 18. Bf5 Nc5 (18... Nxd5 19. Bxh6! gxh6 20. Rhg1+ Kh8 21. Qd2 Qh4 22. Qxd5 $16 Qf4+ $140 23. Kb2 Qxf5 24. Re6 Qf4 25. Qd4+! $18) 19. Rhg1 {[%mdl 128]} Kh8 20. Rg6 Rf7 21. Reg1?! (21. Bxh6 gxh6 22. Rxh6+ Nh7 23. Rxh7+ Rxh7 24. Bxh7 Qf6 {, and Black consolidates his position.}) (21. Qd2 $142 ! Qf8! 22. Qd4 $16 (22. Bxh6 $143 Nd3+ 23. Bxd3 cxd3)) 21... Qf8 22. Be3 Nxd5? {Greediness is punished! Black could have successfully defended by means of} (22... Nh5! 23. Be4 (23. Be6 Rf6) 23... Nf4 (23... Nd7!?)) 23. Bd4 (23. Bxc5 dxc5 (23... Rxf5 24. Bd4) 24. Be6 {, winning an exchange, was also possible, e.g.} Nf4 25. Bxf7 Qxf7 26. Rxg7 Nd3+ 27. Kb1 Qxg7 28. Rxg7 Kxg7 29. Qa4! {, and Black's fortress can hardly be held.}) 23... Nf6 24. Qd2 Re8 25. Rxg7 Qxg7 26. Rxg7 Kxg7 27. Qf4 Nd3+ 28. Bxd3 cxd3 29. Kd2 Kg6 30. Kxd3 Re6 31. h4 Rfe7? {[%mdl 8192]} (31... Rh7! {was the only way to avoid further material losses although White should win in the long run.}) 32. h5+! Kf7 33. Qf5 {[%cal Rf5g6]} Re5 34. Qg6+ Ke6 35. f4 {The capitulation was a bit premature. Black probably didn't see the only defence} (35. f4 Rd7 $8 (35... Rf5? 36. Bxf6 Rxf6 37. f5+ Ke5 38. f4+) {although his position after} 36. fxe5 (36. Qxh6!? Rf5 37. Qg6 Rxf4 38. h6) 36... dxe5 37. Qxh6 exd4 38. cxd4 Rd5 39. Qe3+ Kf7 40. h6 {is surely lost.}) 1-0

