{[%evp 0,55,32,4,42,18,39,15,25,-17,52,51,52,52,52,31,41,15,43,23,23,13,38,38,0,3,18,-20,-72,-118,-134,-173,-173,-149,-149,-195,-181,-257,-162,-72,-72,-143,57,206,206,156,156,102,387,387,416,382,29985,29986,29987,29988,29989,29990]} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. d3 h6 5. Nc3 Bb4 6. O-O Bxc3 7. bxc3 O-O 8. Bb3 d5 {This time Dubov opens the centre right away.} (8... d6 {was seen in one of the previous games between both players, which I also annotated.}) 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. h3 {A clever idea... if Black doesn't find how to meet it!} (10. Re1 Bg4 $13) 10... Nxc3 11. Qe1 Nd4! {Refuting White's concept.} 12. Nxe5 (12. Qxc3?? Ne2+ $19) 12... Nce2+ 13. Kh1 (13. Kh2 {was a better move, to avoid the trick we saw in the game. Of course, Black is more than fine anyway.}) 13... Bxh3! 14. gxh3 Nxb3 15. Qxe2? (15. axb3 Qd5+ $19) 15... Qd5+ 16. Kh2 Nxa1 17. Bb2 {Luckily for Magnus (unless he had planned everything?), White does have some compensation.} Rae8 (17... Nxc2!? 18. Qxc2 Rfe8 19. Ng4 Qd6+! {is also better for Black according to the engine, but I have to say it looks unclear.}) (17... Qd6!? 18. f4 Rae8 19. Qf2 Nxc2 20. Qxc2 f6 21. Ng6 Rf7 {should be an improved version of the above line.}) 18. Rg1 f6 (18... Qd6 19. Rg3! $44 (19. Qg4? g6 $19)) 19. Qg4 g5 20. Qf5 Re7? {Declining a draw vs the World Champion to play a losing move!} (20... Rxe5 21. Qg6+ Kh8 $11) 21. Ng6 Qd6+ 22. Rg3 Nxc2? {Two serious mistakes (almost) in a row are too many against Carlsen!} (22... Re1 23. Nxf8 Kxf8 24. Bxf6 Qf4 $8 25. Bg7+! $16) 23. Nxf8 Nd4 (23... Kxf8? 24. Bxf6 Rf7? 25. Qc8+ $18) (23... Ne3 24. fxe3 Rxe3 25. Qg6+ Kxf8 26. Qxf6+ Qxf6 27. Bxf6 $18) 24. Bxd4 Qxd4 25. Ne6 Qe5 26. Qg6+ Kh8 27. Qxh6+ Kg8 28. Qf8+ 1-0

