1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 b5 4. cxb5 a6 5. bxa6 g6 6. Nc3 Bxa6 {After Adams and Topalov stopped playing the Benko almost a decade ago, the gambit went into a decline and became a very rare guest at the higher level. Therefore Bologan using it in Biel no less than 3 times came as a surprise. Although it brought the out-of-form Moldavian GM only grief, the positions were perhaps not so clear as the results indicate.} 7. e4 ({Another important line is} 7. g3 d6 8. Nf3 Bg7 9. Bg2 O-O 10. Rb1 {and now:} Nbd7 (10... Bc8 11. Nd2!? Bf5 12. e4 Bc8?! (12... Bg4 13. Qc2 Na6 14. a3 Qc8 15. Nc4 Rb8 16. Na5 Bd7 17. O-O c4 18. Nc6 Bxc6 19. dxc6 e6 20. Rd1 Ng4 21. Bg5 Qc7 {Happel,H (2254)-Kohler,A (2298)/Amsterdam/2002/} 22. a4!? $36 {[%cal Rc3b5]}) {was an unusual novelty, but White quickly returned the pawn for a powerful initiative after} 13. O-O Ba6 14. Re1 Nfd7 15. Nf3 Bc4 16. Bf4! Nb6 17. e5 Bxa2 18. Ra1 Bxd5 19. Nxd5 Rxa1 20. Nxe7+ Qxe7 21. Qxa1 d5 22. e6! fxe6 23. Bh3 e5 24. Nxe5 Qf6 25. Qa7 $18 {,Wang,H (2739)-Bologan,V (2732)/Biel/2012/}) 11. O-O Qa5 {is the more customary choice:} 12. Bd2 (12. Qc2 Nb6 13. Rd1 Nfd7 14. Bd2 Nc4 15. Be1 Rfb8 16. Qc1 Nde5 17. Nxe5 Nxe5 18. h3 Bc8 19. b3 c4 20. f4 Nd7 21. Qe3 cxb3 22. axb3 Qd8 23. Na4 Nf6 24. Bf2 Bf5 25. Rbc1 Rb4 26. g4 Bd7 27. Rc6 Rab8 28. Rd3 {Korobov,A (2660)-Caruana,F (2736)/Moscow/2012/} h5!? $13) 12... Bb7 (12... Rfb8 13. Qc2 {Kramnik,V (2807)-Topalov,V (2743)/Wijk aan Zee/2003/ This game seriously affected the popularity of the whole Benko Gambit. See the more detailed notes in CBM 93}) 13. Qc2 Qa7!? 14. e4 Ba6 15. Rfd1 Ng4 16. Be1 Rfb8 17. b3 Nge5 18. Nxe5 Nxe5 19. h3?! (19. a4! $13 {/}) 19... c4 $36 20. b4 Nd3 21. a3?! (21. b5 $142 $132) 21... Bc8 22. Ra1 Bd7 23. Ra2 Qd4 24. Ne2 Nxe1 25. Nxd4? (25. Rxe1 Qd3 $36) 25... Nxc2 26. Nxc2 Ba4 $19 {[%cal Ra4b3] Le Quang,L (2693)-Bologan,V (2732)/Astana blitz/2012/}) 7... Bxf1 8. Kxf1 d6 9. Nf3 Bg7 10. g3 O-O 11. Kg2 Nbd7 12. Qe2 {A rare idea, which Carlsen connects with the plan of building an outpost on b5. It also stops the a6, a8, e6 plan, which Black employed after the more usual moves.} ({These are} 12. Re1) ({or} 12. h3 {The two continuations occurred in an absolute majority of the games which feature our position. As White mostly plays both moves in quick succession, the lines often transpose into each other.}) 12... Qb6 ({The typical Benko move is} 12... Qa5 {, but perhaps it's not ideal:} 13. Bd2!? (13. a4 Rfb8 {prevents b5 for the time being...} 14. Bd2?! (14. Ra3 $142 !?) 14... Rxb2! 15. Nd1 Rxd2 16. Nxd2 Nxe4 (16... Nxd5!? $36) 17. Nc4 Qb4 18. Ndb2? (18. Rc1 $13) 18... Nc3 19. Qxe7 Ne5! 20. Qxd6 Nxc4 21. Qc6 Ne3+ 22. fxe3 Qe4+ 23. Kh3 Qf5+ 24. Kg2 Rb8 $19 {Ramirez,A (2559)-Leon Hoyos,M (2579)/Vancouver/2012/}) (13. e5 dxe5 14. Nxe5 Nxe5 15. Qxe5 Ra7 (15... Rfd8! $44 {[%cal Rf6d5] shows up White's 13th move as rather premature.}) 16. Rd1 Rd8 17. Qe2 Rad7 18. Qf3 c4 19. Be3 Nxd5 20. Nxd5 Rxd5 21. Rxd5 (21. Bb6! $14) 21... Qxd5 22. Qxd5 Rxd5 23. Rc1 Bxb2 24. Rxc4 Ba3 25. Rc3 Ra5 $11 {Carlsen,M (2837)-Andreikin,D (2700)/Astana blitz/2012/}) (13. Bf4 Ng4 14. Nd2 Nge5 15. Bxe5 (15. Be3 Rfb8 16. f4? Ng4 17. Qxg4 Rxb2 18. Ne2 Rxd2 19. Bxd2 Qxd2 20. Rad1 Qc2 $17 {Gerusel,M-Pedersen,K/Grossenbrode 1971/}) 15... Bxe5!? (15... Nxe5 16. f4 Nd7 17. Nc4 $14) 16. Nc4 Qa6 17. Nxe5 Qxe2 18. Nxe2 Nxe5 19. b3 Rfb8 (19... Ra3 $44) 20. Rhc1 Nd3?! 21. Rc3 Nb4 22. a3 Ra7 23. Kf1 Rba8 24. a4 Rb8 25. f3 Rab7 26. Ke1 $14 {Yarmonov,I (2324)-Matijasevic,I (2104)/Split/2012/ The Ukrainian IM Yarmonov often plays the 12.e2 line.}) 13... Rab8 (13... Qb4 14. Rab1 Rfb8 15. Rhc1 Ng4 16. b3 Qa3 17. Ne1! Ngf6 18. Nc2 Qa6 19. Qxa6 Rxa6 20. f3 Ne8 21. a4 Nc7 22. Na3 Ne5 23. Ncb5 Nxb5 24. Nxb5 $16 {Yarmonov,I (2277)-Cocogne,L (1965)/Turin/2006/ In this game White achieved his strategic ideal.}) 14. b3 Qa8 15. Rac1 $14 e6?! 16. dxe6 fxe6 17. Bf4 Rb6 18. Rhd1 d5 19. Ne5 Ra6 20. a4 Nxe4 21. Nxe4 Bxe5 22. Bxe5 Nxe5 23. Nxc5 d4+ 24. Qe4 $18 {Horvath,C (2505)-Gibicar,D (2085)/Vienna/2012/}) (12... Ng4!? 13. Nd2 Ngf6 14. Nc4 Nb6 15. a4 Nxc4 16. Qxc4 Qa5 17. Bd2 (17. Nb5 Rfb8 {[%cal Rb8b5] } 18. Ra3 Qb4! $132) 17... Rfb8 18. Ra2 Nd7 19. Qe2 Qa6 20. Qxa6 Rxa6 21. Rb1 Rb4 (21... c4!? $44 {[%cal Yd7c5]}) 22. b3 c4 23. Rab2 (23. bxc4 $142 Rxc4 24. Rb7 $14) 23... cxb3? (23... h5 24. bxc4 Rxc4 $11) 24. Rxb3 Rxb3 25. Rxb3 Kf8 26. Rb4 $14 {Yarmonov,I (2340)-Tocklin,T (1885)/Bialystok/2010/}) (12... Qc7 13. Bf4 Rfb8 14. Rab1 Rb6 15. Rhc1 Qb7 16. Rc2 e6 (16... Nh5 17. Bd2 Bxc3 18. Bxc3 Rxa2 $132) 17. Rd1 (17. dxe6 fxe6 18. Bxd6!? Rxd6 19. e5 $14) 17... exd5 18. exd5 Re8 19. Qd2 Ne4 20. Nxe4 Rxe4 21. b3 Nf6 22. Qd3 Qe7 23. Bg5 h6 24. Bxf6 Bxf6 25. Rc4 $14 {Yarmonov,I (2340)-Matijasevic,I (2101)/Bialystok/2010/}) 13. a4!? (13. h3 e6!? 14. Rd1 exd5 15. exd5 Rfe8 16. Qb5 (16. Qd3 $142 $14 {/}) 16... Qa7 17. Qc6? Rac8 18. Qxd6 Nh5 19. g4 Ne5! {[%csl Rd6][%cal Rc8d8]} 20. gxh5 Nxf3? (20... Rcd8 $17) 21. Qg3 Nd4 22. Bf4 Qb7 23. Rab1 Rcd8 24. Kh2 $14 {Tregubov,P (2545)-Barkhagen,J (2400)/Gausdal/1994/}) (13. Re1 Rfb8 14. e5 Nxe5 15. Nxe5 dxe5 16. Qxe5 Rb7 17. Qe2 Ne8 18. Bd2 Nd6 19. b3 Qa6! 20. Rac1 Qxe2 21. Rxe2 c4 $44 {½,Sosonko,G (2525)-Topalov,V (2670)/Polanica Zdroj/1995/}) (13. Rd1 Qa6!? {A typical Benko motif - the queen swap limits White's attacking potential without reducing Black's queenside chances.} (13... Rfb8 14. Rb1 Ne8 15. Bd2 Qa6!? 16. Qe3 Nc7 17. b3 Rb7 18. Qg5 Bf6 19. Qh6 Nb5 20. Nxb5 Qxb5 21. a4 Qd3 22. Qe3 Qxe3 (22... Qc2!?) 23. Bxe3 Rab8 24. Nd2 Bc3 $132 {Muse,D (2230)-Boehle,L/Bundesliga/1991/}) 14. Qc2 (14. Qxa6 Rxa6 15. Nd2 Rb8 16. a3 Nb6 17. Ra2 Ng4 18. Ne2 f5! 19. h3 Ne5 20. Nf4 Na4 21. exf5 gxf5 22. Re1 c4 23. Nf1 Bh6! $15 {Ivanov,I (2515)-Alburt,L (2570)/Hastings/1983/}) 14... Ng4 15. h3 Nge5 16. Nxe5 Nxe5 17. b3 (17. Be3 Nc4 18. Rac1 Rfb8 19. b3 Na3 20. Qd2 c4 21. Qe2 h6 22. bxc4 Nxc4 23. Rc2 Na3 24. Qxa6 Rxa6 25. Rcc1 Rb4 $11 {Gerusel,M (2425)-Giorgadze,T (2535)/Dortmund/1979/}) 17... Rab8 18. Rb1 Rfc8 19. Be3 Qa5 (19... Rb4!? $44 {[%cal Yc5c4]}) 20. Ne2 Qb4?! 21. Bd2 Qb5 22. Bc3 $36 {Kristiansen,E (2220)-Finnlaugsson,G (2072)/Reykjavik/2011/}) 13... Rfb8 (13... Ng4?! 14. Nd2 Ngf6 15. Nc4 Qb4 16. Bd2 Nb6 17. Nxb6 Qxb6 18. Nb5 e6 19. Bc3 exd5 20. exd5 Rfe8 21. Qf3 Nd7 22. Rhe1 Ne5 23. Bxe5 (23. Qd1!? $16) 23... Rxe5 24. Rxe5 Bxe5 25. Qe2 $14 {Thorfinnsson,B (2421)-Rodriguez Guerrero,E (2454)/England/2012/}) 14. Nb5 ({In the last round we saw} 14. Bd2 Ne8 (14... Qb3 15. Rhb1 $14 e6? 16. Ra3 Qb7 17. dxe6 fxe6 18. Bf4 Qc6 19. Rd1 e5 20. Qc4+ Kh8 21. Ng5 $18 {Bhat,V (2549)-Tirard,H (2451)/Metz/2010/}) 15. Rhb1 Nc7 16. Nd1 $146 (16. Ra3 Qa6 17. Qd1 Ne5!? (17... Nb6 18. b3 $14) 18. Nxe5 Bxe5 19. Qc2 Rb6 20. Nd1 Rab8 21. Bc3 Bxc3 22. Rxc3 (22. Nxc3 $142 Qa5 23. b3 Rb4 $44) 22... Rb4 23. b3 Qb7 24. Rb2 f5 25. f3 fxe4 26. fxe4 e6 $36 {½,Elsness,F (2499)-Byklum,B (2251)/NOR-chT/2012/}) 16... Qa6 17. Qxa6 Rxa6 18. a5 f5 19. exf5 Nxd5 (19... gxf5 $142 20. Nh4 (20. Ne3 f4 21. gxf4 Nf6 $13) 20... f4!? 21. Bxf4 Nxd5 22. Bd2 e6 $14 {/}) 20. fxg6 hxg6 21. Ra4 Nb4 22. Ne3 Rb5 23. b3 e6 24. Bxb4 Rxb4 25. Rxb4 cxb4 26. Rc1! $14 {,Nakamura,H (2778)-Bologan,V (2732)/Biel/2012/}) 14... Ne8 15. Bg5 $146 ({The developing text move seems more to the point than} 15. Nd2 Qa6 16. Ra3 Nc7 17. Re1 Nxb5 18. axb5 Qb7 (18... Qb6!? {} 19. Nb1 Ra5 20. Rxa5 Qxa5 21. Na3 Qb4 $44) 19. Nb1! $14 Rxa3 20. Nxa3 Nb6 21. Rd1 Re8 22. f3 Qa8 23. Qc2 Bd4 24. Rd3 e6?! 25. dxe6 fxe6 26. Be3 $16 {Aliavdin,N (2382)-Licznerski,L (2269)/Lazy/2012/}) 15... Qd8 (15... h6?! 16. Bxe7 Rb7 (16... f6? 17. Nh4 Kf7 18. Nxg6! Kxg6 19. Qg4+ $18) 17. Nd2 Ne5 18. f4 Rxe7 19. fxe5 Bxe5 20. Nc4 Qd8 21. Rhf1 Nc7 22. Nxc7 Qxc7 23. a5 Rae8 24. a6 Bg7 25. a7 Ra8 26. Ra6 $16 {Shaw,P (2168)-Ledger,S (2089)/GBR-ch North Shields/2012/ Curiously enough, this game was played on the same day!}) (15... Kf8 16. Qc2 {[%cal Yf3d2,Yd2c4]} Nc7 17. Nxc7 Qxc7 18. Rab1 $14 {[%cal Yb2b3,Yg5d2,Yd2c3]}) 16. Ra3 (16. Ra2 h6 (16... Nc7!? {} 17. Bxe7 Qxe7 18. Nxc7 Ra5 {[%cal Rb8b7]} 19. Rha1 Nf6 20. Nb5 Qxe4 $13) 17. Bd2 Nc7 18. Nxc7 (18. Rha1 Nxb5 19. axb5 Rxa2 20. Rxa2 Qb6 21. Bc3 Nf6 22. Nd2 Nd7!? $132) 18... Qxc7 19. Rb1 Rb3 $44) 16... Nb6 {Black ignores play on the b-file and starts a more complex plan of undermining White's centre.} ({However, this backfires in the end, so} 16... h6 17. Bf4 Nc7 18. Rha1 (18. Nc3!?) 18... Ra5 $14 {[%cal Gb8b2] / possibly promises better counterchances.}) 17. b3 (17. a5!? Nd7 18. Rha1 $14) 17... Qd7 18. Ra2 (18. Rd1 Nxd5!? 19. exd5 Rxb5 20. Qxe7 Qxe7 21. Bxe7 Rb7 $44) 18... f6 {Bologan follows his idea.} (18... h6 19. Bc1 Nc7 {now favours White after} 20. Nxc7 Qxc7 21. Bb2 $36) 19. Bc1 f5 20. exf5 (20. Re1 fxe4 (20... Rb7!?) 21. Qxe4 Nf6 22. Qxe7 Qxe7 23. Rxe7 Nbxd5 {[%cal Rd5e7,Rb8b5]} 24. Ree2 Nb4 $14 {/}) 20... gxf5 (20... Qxf5 21. Rd1 {also doesn't solve Black's problems:} Nf6 (21... Nxd5 22. Qc4 Rxb5 (22... e6 23. g4 Qf6 24. Ng5 Rxb5 25. Qxb5 Nf4+ (25... Nc3 26. Qb7 Nc7 27. Qxc7 Nxa2 28. Be3 $18) 26. Kg3 Nc7 27. Qc4 $16) 23. axb5 Rxa2 24. Rxd5 Qf7 (24... Qc2 25. Qxc2 Rxc2 26. b6 Nf6 27. Bg5! Nd7 $8 28. Bxe7 Nxb6 29. Rxd6 $18 {[%csl Rb6]}) 25. b6 e6 26. Rd3 $16 {[%cal Rb3b4,Yf3g5]}) (21... Bf6 22. h3 $16 {[%cal Yg3g4,Yc1b2] } Nxd5 23. Qc4 Rxb5 (23... e6 24. g4 Qb1 25. Re2 $18) 24. axb5 Rxa2 25. Rxd5 Qe6 26. b6 $40) 22. Qxe7 (22. Nc7!? $36) 22... Nfxd5 23. Qe1 $16 {[%csl Rd6]}) 21. Rd1 Nf6 22. Qe6+ Qxe6 23. dxe6 $16 {[%csl Ge6,Re7,Rf5] Although Black's pieces are active, he can't effectively attack the advanced e6-pawn and this in connection with the weakness on f5 (both pawn and square) and consequently e7 give White a sizeable advantage.} Ne4 (23... f4 24. Bxf4 Nbd5 {[%cal Rb8b5]} 25. Rc2 Nxf4+ 26. gxf4 Nh5 27. Rc4 Rf8 28. Nc7 $16) 24. Nh4! {[%mdl 64] In the following short skirmish the tactics work in White's favour.} c4 ({The passive} 24... Rf8 25. a5! {[%csl Ga5]} Ra6 {gives White a pleasant choice:} 26. Ra3 (26. Be3 Nc3 27. Nxc3 Bxc3 28. Bh6 Bg7 29. Bg5 Bf6 30. Bxf6 Rxf6 31. axb6 Rxa2 32. b7 Rf8 33. Nxf5 $18) 26... Na8 27. Ra4 {[%cal Rg3g4]} Nc3 28. Nxc3 Bxc3 29. Rd3 Bd4 30. Rf3 $18) 25. bxc4 Nxc4 {[%cal Rb8b5]} 26. Nc7! Nc3 $8 (26... Ra7 27. Nd5 $18 {[%cal Rh4f5]}) (26... Ra5 27. Nd5 Rxd5 (27... Rb7 28. Nxf5 $18 (28. Rc2!?)) 28. Rxd5 Nc3 29. Rc2 Nxd5 30. Rxc4 $18 {[%csl Ga4][%cal Rh4f5]}) 27. Nxa8 Nxa2 (27... Rxa8 28. Rc2 Nxd1 29. Rxc4 $18) (27... Nxd1 28. Nc7 Nc3 29. Rc2 Rc8 30. Na6 Nxa4 (30... Ra8 31. Nb4 Rxa4 32. Nc6 $18) 31. Nxf5 $16) 28. Nc7 Nc3 ({A more testing move was} 28... Rb1 29. Nxf5 Bf8 (29... Rxc1 30. Rxc1 Nxc1 31. Nxe7+ Kf8 (31... Kh8 32. Ng6+) 32. Ned5 $18) (29... Nxc1 30. Nxe7+ Kh8 31. Ng6+ hxg6 32. e7 Rb8 33. Rxc1 $18) 30. Nd5 Rxc1 31. Rd4 $16 Ne5 32. a5 Rc5 33. a6 Ra5 34. Nfxe7+ Bxe7 35. Nxe7+ Kf8 36. Nd5 $40 {[%csl Ga6,Ge6]}) 29. Rd3 Rc8 (29... Rf8 30. Bg5 $18) 30. Nb5 (30. Nd5!? Nxd5 31. Rxd5 Nb6 32. Rb5 Nxa4 33. Bg5 $18) 30... Nxb5 (30... Nxa4 31. Nxf5 Bf6 32. g4 $16 {/+-}) 31. axb5 Rc5 (31... Ne5 32. Rd1 Bf6 (32... Rc5 33. Bg5 $18 {[%csl Re7]}) 33. Nxf5 (33. Bh6!? {[%csl Rg8]}) 33... Rc5 34. b6 Rb5 35. Ne3!? Rxb6 36. Nd5 $18) 32. Rb3 $18 {Black has managed to save the f5-pawn for the time being, but now he can't cope with the passed b-pawn.} Na5 33. Rb1 Bd4 (33... Bf6 34. b6 Nb7 35. Bh6 {[%cal Yb1b3,Yb3f3]} Bxh4 36. Ra1! Ra5 37. Rxa5 Nxa5 38. gxh4 $18 {[%csl Rg8][%cal Yg2b5]}) 34. b6 Nb7 35. Rb4 Bxf2 (35... Bf6 36. Bh6 Bxh4 37. Ra4 $18 {and White wins as in the previous note.}) (35... Be5 36. Be3 $18) 36. Kxf2 Rc2+ 37. Kf3 Rxc1 38. Nxf5 Rf1+ (38... Kf8 39. Ra4 Rc8 40. Rf4 $18) 39. Kg4 Nc5 (39... Re1 40. Rc4 Rxe6 41. Rc7 $18) 40. b7 (40. b7 h5+ 41. Kg5 Nxe6+ 42. Kh6 $18) 1-0

