1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. cxd5 Nxd5 5. e4 Nxc3 6. bxc3 Bg7 7. Bc4 c5 8. Ne2 Nc6 9. Be3 O-O 10. O-O Qc7 11. Rc1 Rd8 12. h3 {A relatively rare move, Did White want to avoid} (12. Bf4 Be5!? {?}) 12... a6 (12... b6 {is usually played. Other options are}) (12... e6 {and}) (12... Na5) 13. Bf4 $146 {Or else:} (13. f4 b5 14. Bb3 (14. Bd3 e6 15. f5 exf5 16. exf5 c4 17. Bb1 Re8 18. Bf4 Qd8 19. fxg6 hxg6 20. Ng3 Bb7 21. Qg4 b4 $132 {0-1 Gontcharov,V (2359)-Valdes,L (2365)/Dos Hermanas 2004/CBM 099 ext (45)}) 14... Na5 15. f5 Nxb3 16. Qxb3 gxf5 17. exf5 Bb7 18. Rf4 Bd5 19. Qc2 Kh8 $13 {1-0 Alexandrova,O (2400)-Sulypa,A (2449)/Alushta 2000/CBM 075 ext (39)}) (13. Bb3 b5 (13... Na5 $143 14. Bf4 Qd7 15. dxc5 Nxb3 16. axb3 a5 17. Qc2 Qb5 18. Be3 a4 19. bxa4 Rxa4 20. Rfd1 Re8 21. Nd4 $14 {1/2 Gligoric,S (2575)-Hort,V (2600)/Siegen 1970/EXT 2002 (25)}) 14. Qe1 e6 15. f4 c4 16. Bc2 f5! 17. g4 Ne7 18. Ng3 a5 $132 {0-1 Berta,K (2205)-Feher,G (2445)/Budapest 1998/EXT 2002 (49)}) 13... Qa5! ({Now} 13... Be5 {is rather senseless due to} 14. Bxe5 Nxe5 15. Bb3 Bxh3?! (15... Ng4 {is impossible!}) 16. f4) (13... Qd7 14. dxc5!?) 14. Qb3 e6 15. a4 {White finds nothing better than this pawn sacrifice, with the hope of being able to use his development advantage. However, Black equalizes without any problems.} (15. d5 b5! {(without 12.h3 a6 this would be impossible)} 16. dxc6 bxc4 17. Qxc4 e5 {[%cal Rc8e6]} 18. Be3 Be6 19. Qxc5 Qxc5 20. Bxc5 Rdc8 $44) 15... cxd4 16. cxd4 Nxd4 17. Nxd4 Rxd4 18. Be3!? Rd6 {Black doesn't dare to take the second pawn:} (18... Rxe4 19. Qd3 (19. Rfd1 Bf6) (19. Bb6 Qg5) 19... Rh4 (19... Re5?! 20. Rfd1 Bf6 21. Bd4) 20. Rfd1 ({White can force a draw by means of} 20. Bd2 Qb6 21. Be3 Qa5 ({but not} 21... Bd4?! 22. a5 Qa7? 23. g3! Bxe3 24. fxe3 $18 {[%cal Rd3d8,Rd8f6,Rg3h4]})) 20... Bf6 21. Bb3 $44 {[%csl Ra8,Gc1,Rc8,Gd1,Rh4]}) 19. Rfd1 Rxd1+ 20. Rxd1 b5! {The simplest. Black gives the pawn back liquidating into a drawish endgame.} 21. axb5 axb5 22. Qxb5 Qxb5 23. Rd8+ Bf8 24. Bxb5 Bb7 25. Rxa8 Bxa8 26. f3 f5 27. Bd3 fxe4 28. Bxe4 Bxe4 29. fxe4 Kf7 30. Kf1 h5 31. Kg1 Bd6 32. Kf1 Bf8 33. Kg1 Bd6 34. Kf1 Bf8 1/2-1/2

