{[%evp 0,68,22,22,22,22,22,12,11,-24,-14,-9,-13,-11,-1,-26,-19,-26,-12,-22,-13,-11,-11,-14,20,4,9,-18,-23,-30,-8,-41,-34,-23,29,7,-25,-27,-27,-111,-133,-112,-135,-157,-156,-197,-179,-179,-163,-148,-166,-146,-120,-138,-147,-147,-259,-255,-294,-295,-287,-299,-293,-475,-298,-280,-265,-332,-338,-347,-380]} {It is one main question,which face strong IGMs ,playing Carlsen with White-to follow theoretical lines or try to take him out of the theory?Korobovs chice is terribly wrong, as World Champion is much stronger than him in nontheoretical positions!  It is one main question,which face strong IGMs ,playing Carlsen with White-to follow theoretical lines or try to take him out of the theory?Korobovs chice is terribly wrong, as World Champion is much stronger than him in nontheoretical positions!} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 d5 3. e3 a6 4. b3 ({Carlsen had it before} 4. c4 e6 5. b3 c5 6. Bb2 cxd4 7. exd4 Nc6 8. Nbd2 g6 9. Bd3 (9. Be2 Bg7 10. O-O O-O 11. Ne5 Nd7 12. Nxc6 bxc6 13. Nf3 Qa5 14. Qc2 Bb7 15. Rfd1 Rfc8 16. Bc3 Qc7 17. Qd2 Nf6 18. Ba5 Ne4 19. Bxc7 Nxd2 20. Bb6 Nxf3+ 21. Bxf3 Bh6 {1/2-1/2 (21) Polugaevsky, L (2605)-Kortschnoj,V (2625) Antwerp 1993}) 9... Bg7 10. O-O O-O 11. Rc1 b6 12. Re1 Bb7 13. a3 Rc8 14. Qe2 dxc4 15. bxc4 Re8 16. h3 Qc7 17. Qe3 Ne7 18. Ne5 Nf5 19. Bxf5 exf5 20. Ndf3 Bxf3 21. Qxf3 Ne4 {with great play, Radjabov,T (2738)-Carlsen,M (2850) Berlin 2015}) 4... Bf5 5. Ba3 e6 ({Another set up was} 5... Nbd7 6. Nbd2 e6 7. Bxf8 Nxf8) 6. Bxf8 Kxf8 7. Be2 Nc6 ({To slight White advantage let opening of the center} 7... c5 8. dxc5 Qa5+ 9. Nbd2 Nc6 10. a3 Qxc5 11. c4) 8. O-O h5! 9. c4 {As explained FM Luca Barillaro,who cooperated with Yan Nepomniashchi during his mach against Magnus,this kind of play with powerful flank diversions ,is the result of Magnus work with Alpha zero!} h4 10. Nc3 ({Such pawns had to be stopped} 10. h3 g5 (10... Ne4 11. Qc1 Rh6 12. Nc3 Rg6 13. Kh1 Kg8 14. Nd2 Nxd2 15. Qxd2) 11. Nh2 ({questions are not answered even aftera} 11. Nxg5 Rg8 12. f4) 11... Rg8 12. Nc3 Ne7 13. Ng4 {with nice safe game.}) 10... Ne4 ({Black initiative would be stucked after} 10... h3 11. g3 Qe7 12. Ne5 Nxe5 13. dxe5 Ne4 14. Nxe4 dxe4 15. Qc2 g5 16. Rfd1 Kg7 17. Qc3) 11. Rc1 ({Better was to try to fix the structure,which is seriousely better for White} 11. Nxe4 Bxe4 12. h3 Rh6 13. Bd3 f5 14. Bxe4 dxe4 15. Nh2 Qg5 16. Qe2 Kg8 17. f3) 11... Rh6 12. cxd5 ({More logical was} 12. h3 Kg8 13. Bd3) 12... exd5 13. Nd2 ({still better structure promised} 13. Nxe4 dxe4 14. Nd2 Qd7 15. h3 Bxh3 (15... Rg6 16. Kh2) 16. Nxe4 Rg6 17. Bf3 Bxg2 18. Bxg2 h3 19. Ng3) 13... Nxc3 14. Rxc3 Qd6 ({It was nice Knight manoevre to get useful transfer} 14... Na7 15. Rc1 Nb5 16. Bg4 Bxg4 17. Qxg4 h3 18. g3 Nd6) 15. Qc1?! ({Prophylactical measures were necessary} 15. h3 Rg6 16. Kh1 Qd7 17. Kh2) 15... Re8 16. Bf3 Re7 17. Rc5 {[#]} Nb4! 18. Nc4?! {Wrong idea to place Knight out of the game.Better was} (18. Qa1 b6 19. Rc3 h3 20. g3 c5 21. Rfc1 Nd3 {but Black has overtake the initiative here.}) 18... Qe6 19. Nb2 ({Nothing promised} 19. Ne5 f6) 19... h3 20. g3 Nxa2 21. Qd2 Be4 22. Be2 b6! 23. Na4 Bh7 24. Re1 Qe4! 25. f3 Qxe3+ 26. Qxe3 Rxe3 27. Rxc7 Rhe6 {Creating the decisive pin} 28. Kf2 Bd3 29. Bxd3 Rxe1 30. g4 ({Nothing changed} 30. Bxa6 Rh1 31. g4 Rxh2+ 32. Kg3 Rd2 33. Kxh3 g5!) 30... Nb4 31. Bf5 R1e2+ ({It was no big difference with which Rook to attack} 31... R6e2+ 32. Kg3 g5) 32. Kg3 Rd6 33. Rb7 ({Other moves just prolonged suffering} 33. g5 g6 34. Bxh3 Re7 35. Rc8+ Kg7 36. Rb8 Nc2) 33... g6 34. Bd7 g5 0-1

