1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. g3 Bb7 5. Bg2 Be7 6. O-O O-O 7. Re1 Na6 8. Ne5 Bxg2 9. Kxg2 c6 {This move is apparently too slow.} (9... Qc8) 10. e4 ({Here is an example of Black taking the initiative:} 10. Nc3 Qc8 11. Bg5 h6 12. Bxf6 Bxf6 13. Ne4 Be7 14. Qb3 d6 15. Nd3 Nc7 16. Nc3 b5 17. c5?! dxc5 18. Nxc5 e5 19. e3 exd4 20. exd4 Bxc5 21. dxc5 Qf5 22. Ne4 Ne6 23. Qc3 Rad8 $15 {0-1 Molnar,P-Maiorov,N/Kharkov 2007/CBM 117 ext (63)}) 10... Qc7 11. Nc3 Qb7 12. Nd3 (12. Nf3 b5 13. c5 Ne8 14. Bf4 b4 15. Na4 f5 16. Nd2 fxe4 17. Nxe4 Nac7 18. Be5 Nd5 19. Rc1 Nef6 20. f3 Qc8 21. Nd6 Qa6 22. b3 Bxd6 23. Bxd6 Rf7 24. Qe2 Qa5 25. Qd2 Ne8 26. Be5 Nec7 27. a3 Nb5 28. axb4 Qxb4 29. Qxb4 Nxb4 30. Re3 Nd5 31. Rd3 Raf8 32. Nb2 Nb4 {½-½ Brodsky,M-Chernyshov,K/Dagomys RUS 2008/The Week in Chess 702}) (12. Qf3 Rad8 13. Bf4 d5 14. exd5 cxd5 15. Bg5 h6 16. Bxf6 Bxf6 17. cxd5 exd5 18. Rad1 Nc7 19. Ng4 Rd6 20. Qf5 Rfd8 21. Rd3 $14 {½-½ Greenfeld,A-Rozentalis,E/Panormo 2001/CBM 084 ext (45)}) 12... d5 13. e5 Nd7 14. cxd5 cxd5 15. h4 Nb4 16. Bg5 {A typical manoeuvre - the exchange of bishops in order to open up the h-file. Of course, Black avoids that.} Nxd3 17. Qxd3 Bb4 18. Rec1 a6 19. Ne2 Rfc8 20. h5 h6 21. a3 Bf8 22. Bd2 Rxc1 23. Rxc1 Rc8 24. Rf1 {[%cal Yf2f4,Yf4f5]} b5 25. f4 Qc6 26. Rc1 Qb7 27. Rf1 Qc6 28. Qf3 Qb6 {Start of a wrong plan.} (28... Nb6 $142 29. f5 exf5 30. Qxf5 Qe6 31. Qf3 $14) 29. f5 exf5 30. Bc3 {[%cal Rf3d5]} a5? {Overlooking a tactical blow.} (30... Qc6 31. g4 $16) 31. Bxa5! {[%mdl 64]} (31. Qxd5 {was not bad either.}) 31... Qxa5 32. Qxf5 Qd2 (32... Qd8 33. Qxf7+ Kh7 34. Nf4 $18) 33. Qxf7+ Kh8 34. Rf2 Rd8 35. Qxd5 {[%cal Re5e6,Re2f4]} Qa5 36. Nf4 Qa8 37. Ng6+ (37. Ng6+ Kh7 38. Qxa8 Rxa8 39. Rf7 $18) 1-0

