1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e3 O-O 5. Ne2 d5 6. cxd5 exd5 7. g3 Re8 8. Bg2 Bf8 ({The immediate} 8... c6 {is more popular here.}) 9. O-O Na6!? {A curious concept.} (9... c6) 10. a3 (10. h3!? c6 11. g4 h6 12. Ng3 Nc7 13. f4 g6 14. Qf3 b5 15. a3 a5 16. g5 Nh7 17. h4 hxg5 18. fxg5 Be6 19. Nce2 Qd7 20. Qf2 Bg7 21. Bd2 Bg4 22. Nf4 Ne6 $132 {1-0 Kohlweyer,B (2443)-Chuchelov,V (2539)/Belgium 2001/CBM 081 ext (55)}) 10... c6 11. f3 (11. b3?! Bf5 (11... Nc7 12. Ra2 Bf5 13. f3 h6 14. Nf4 c5! 15. Nce2 b6 16. g4 Bh7 17. Ng3 Nb5 $36 {0-1 Lerner,K (2525)-Garcia Gonzales,G (2515)/Jurmala 1983/MCD (40)}) 12. Ra2 Qd7 13. f3 h5 14. Nf4 Bd6 15. Nxh5 Nxh5 16. g4 Bg6 17. gxh5 Bxh5 $17 {1/2 Panczyk,K (2365)-Volzhin,A (2530)/Wisla 1998/EXT 2000 (22)}) (11. h3 Nc7 12. g4 Bd6 13. f4 Bxg4?! (13... h6 $15) 14. hxg4 Nxg4 15. Rf3 Qh4 16. Bh3 Re6 17. Bxg4 Rg6 18. Rg3 Rxg4 19. Kg2 $14 {1-0 Tatai,S (2435)-Ivkov,B (2475)/Torremolinos 1983/MCD (60)}) (11. Nf4 Nc7 12. b4 a6 13. Ra2 (13. f3?! Nb5! 14. Nxb5 axb5 15. Bd2 Nd7 16. e4 dxe4 17. fxe4 Nf6 18. Bc3 Nxe4 $19 {1-0 Straeter,T (2345)-Ernst,S (2512)/Germany 2006/EXT 2007 (58)}) 13... Bf5 14. f3 Nb5 15. Nxb5 axb5 $15 {0-1 Maksimovic,S (2225)-Prudnikova,S (2405)/Belgrade 1995/EXT 1997 (48)}) 11... c5!? {A standard reaction to f2-f3.} 12. g4 h6 (12... Nc7!? 13. b3?! (13. g5 $142 Nd7 14. f4 Nb6 15. dxc5 Bxc5 16. Qd3 Nc4 17. Nd4 $13) 13... a5 14. Ng3 h6 15. Ra2 b5 16. Kh1 c4 $17 {0-1 Moutousis,K (2475)-Mastrovasilis,A (2315)/Panormo 1998/CBM 067 ext (46)}) 13. h3 b6 14. Ng3 Bb7 15. f4 Rc8 $15 {Black has good development; White's attacking chances are slim.} 16. g5 hxg5! (16... Ne4 17. Ncxe4 dxe4 18. gxh6 g6 (18... cxd4 19. exd4 gxh6 20. f5 $36) 19. h7+!? (19. f5 Bxh6) 19... Kxh7 20. f5 Bg7 $13) 17. fxg5 Ne4! (17... cxd4? 18. exd4 Ne4 19. Ncxe4 dxe4 20. Rxf7! Kxf7 21. g6+! $18 {}) 18. Ncxe4 dxe4 19. Qg4 (19. Rxf7 {now doesn't work as the c1 bishop is not in the attack.}) 19... g6 20. Nxe4 (20. Bxe4!? Bd5!? $36) 20... Bxe4 21. Bxe4 cxd4! {[%cal Ra6c5][%mdl 512]} 22. Bb7 {Obvious but probably wrong!} (22. Qf3 $142 !? Qd7 (22... Qxg5+ 23. Kh1 Rxe4! 24. Qxe4 d3! 25. Qxd3 Nc5 $15) 23. b4 $15 {[%cal Yc1b2]} (23. Bd5 $143 Re7 24. exd4 Bg7 $17)) 22... Rc2! 23. Bxa6 (23. Qf4 Qd7! 24. Bxa6 dxe3 (24... Qxh3? 25. Qxf7+ Kh8 26. Rf2 Qg4+ 27. Kf1 Qd1+ $11) 25. Qg4!? {(recommended by IM Ivan Smikovsky)} (25. Bc4 Rxc4 26. Qxc4 e2 27. Re1 Qxh3 $19) {doesn't help due to} 25... Qd5! 26. Be2 (26. Qf3 Qxf3 27. Rxf3 e2 28. Be3 Bc5! $19) 26... Bc5 $19 {[%cal Ye8e5,Ye5f5] White is nearly in zugzwang!}) 23... Qc7 $17 {Despite White's extra piece, Black is dominating the board.} 24. Qf4 Bd6 25. Qf3 (25. Qg4 $142 dxe3 26. Be2 Bg3! $17 {I.Smikovsky} (26... Re5 $143 27. h4)) 25... Bc5 (25... dxe3! 26. Be2 Re5 27. h4 (27. Qg4 Rxe2!) 27... Rf5 28. Qa8+ Bf8 29. Rxf5 Rxe2! 30. Bxe3 gxf5 $19 {I.Smikovsky}) 26. Qf4 Bd6 27. Qf3 Bc5? (27... dxe3) 28. Qf4 Qxf4 29. Rxf4 dxe3 30. Kf1 e2+ 31. Ke1 Rd8 32. Bxe2 Re8 33. Bd2 Rxd2 34. Kxd2 Be3+ 35. Kc2 Bxf4 36. Bc4 Bxg5 {Black finally has won a pawn but the opposite-coloured bishops eventually enable White to save the game.} 37. Rg1 Re5 38. h4! Bxh4 39. Rxg6+ Kf8 40. Rd6 Re7 41. Bb5 Rc7+ 42. Rc6 Re7 43. Rd6 Re5 44. Bc4 Rf5 45. b4 Ke7 46. Rd5 Rf2+ 47. Rd2 Rf4 48. Bb5 Ke6 49. Re2+ Kf6 50. Rd2 Ke6 51. Re2+ Kf6 52. Rd2 Bf2 53. Rd7 a5 54. bxa5 bxa5 55. a4 Bc5 56. Rd5 Bb4 57. Kd3 Ke6 58. Rd4 Rf3+ 59. Ke2 Ra3 60. Bc4+ Ke5 61. Rd3 Rxd3 1/2-1/2

