{[%evp 0,61,28,12,25,-15,24,23,23,15,23,23,37,-12,22,7,3,-2,12,11,20,29,29,26,24,15,17,19,45,-2,15,-31,-20,-24,-14,-40,-30,-41,1,-2,14,-40,0,-44,-44,-62,-62,-19,-49,-49,-43,-44,-44,-60,-64,-115,-100,-101,-101,-93,-36,-34,-41,-144]} 1. Nf3 Nf6 2. g3 g6 3. Bg2 Bg7 4. O-O O-O 5. d4 d6 6. b3 b5 {A very rare but logical move: Black gains space on the queenside and prepares to bother White's c4 pawn in case of c2-c4 b5xc4 b3xc4.} 7. Bb2 (7. Ne1!? c6 8. c4 bxc4 9. bxc4 Be6 10. Nd2 Qc8 11. e4 Bg4 12. Nef3 Na6 13. Rb1 c5 14. e5 dxe5 15. dxe5 Nd7 (15... Ne8!?) 16. e6 $14 Ne5 17. exf7+ Rxf7? 18. h3! $16 {1-0 (24) Bai,J (2568)-Yanayt,E (2122) Las Vegas 2018}) (7. c4!? {was a normal continuation after all.}) 7... Bb7 8. Nbd2 Nbd7 9. c4 bxc4 10. Nxc4 (10. bxc4 $142 {capturing towards the centre.}) 10... a5! (10... c5 11. dxc5 Nxc5 12. b4 Nce4 13. Rc1 Qd7 14. Na5 Bh6 15. Rc2 Bd5 16. Bxf6 Nxf6 17. Nd4 Rac8 18. Bxd5 Nxd5 19. Ndc6 $14 {0-1 (34) Bistric,F (2325)-Tosic,M (2345) Medulin 1983}) 11. Rc1 c5 12. dxc5 Nxc5 $11 13. Bd4 Ncd7 14. a4?! {[%mdl 32] White wants to fix Black's a5 pawn as a potential weakness but it survives, and White's queenside pawns become motionless.} (14. Qd2 $11) 14... Ra6 15. Na3 Qa8 16. Nb5 Rc6 17. Rxc6 Bxc6 18. Ne1 Bxg2 19. Nxg2 Rc8 20. Na7?! (20. f3!?) 20... Rd8 21. Qc2 e5 22. Be3 d5 23. Nc6 Re8 24. Bd2 Ne4 25. Nxa5 {White has finally won the pawn but his pieces are disorganized.} Rc8 26. Qa2 Ndf6 {[%csl Ra5]} 27. Be1 (27. b4 d4 $17) 27... Nc3! 28. Bxc3 Rxc3 29. b4 Bf8 (29... d4!? $17) 30. Qb2 d4 31. e3 (31. Ne3 $142 !? Ne4! 32. Nec4 d3! 33. exd3 Ng5 34. f3 Rxd3 35. Nxe5 Nxf3+ 36. Nxf3 Rxf3 37. Rxf3 Qxf3 38. Qb3 {keeping drawing chances.}) 31... Ne4! 32. exd4 exd4 33. Nb3 d3 34. Rc1 Rxc1+ 35. Qxc1 Qxa4 36. Qc4 Nc5!? {Nice but} (36... d2 {was winning, too:} 37. Ne3 Qd7 38. Qd4 (38. Nd1 Qg4) 38... Qxd4 39. Nxd4 Nc3 $19) 37. Nd2 Qa1+ (37... Bh6! 38. Nf1 (38. Qxc5 Qa1+ 39. Nf1 d2) 38... d2 39. Nxd2 Bxd2 40. Qxc5 Qa1+ $19) 38. Nf1 d2 39. Ne3 Ne6 40. Qb3 Qe1 41. Kg2 Bxb4 {It is still difficult for Black to convert his extra pawn.} 42. Qb2 h5 43. h4 Ba5 44. Qb8+ Nf8 45. Qa8 Bc3 46. Qc6 Qc1 47. Qd5 Ne6 48. Qc4 Ba5 49. Qd5 Bb4 50. Qb5 Qc3 51. Qd5 Qc1 52. Qb5 Bc3 53. Qa4 Bd4 54. Nd1 Kg7 55. Kf3 Bf6 56. Ke2? (56. Nfe3 {, and White can tenaciously defend.}) 56... Nd4+ 57. Kd3 Qb1+! 58. Kxd2 (58. Ke3 $142 !? {but after} Qf5 59. Nxd2 Be5! {White's king in the centre can hardly survive.}) 58... Qe4! {[%cal Rd4f3]} 0-1

