1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. g3 Bb7 5. Bg2 Be7 6. Nc3 O-O 7. Qc2 c5 8. d5 exd5 9. cxd5 Bxd5 $146 {[%mdl 8]} (9... Nxd5?! {Compared to the popular line (see Radjabov-Leko and Aronian-Anand in this issue), Black has a kind of an "extra tempo" (his bishop has come to b7 in one go) but that tempo has a negative value!} 10. Qe4! (10. Ng5 $143 Bxg5 11. Nxd5 Bxd5 12. Bxd5 Nc6 13. a3 Bxc1 14. Rxc1 Qe7 15. e3 Qe5 16. Rd1 Rad8 17. O-O Ne7 18. e4 Nc6 19. f4 Nd4 20. Qc4 Qe7 $17 {0-1 Tomovic,V-Pirc,V/Zagreb 1949/EXT 2000 (48)}) 10... Nb4 (10... Nxc3 11. Qxb7 {- had White already castled, Black would have taken on e2 with check!}) (10... f5 11. Qc4 b5 12. Qb3 c4 13. Qxb5 $16 {Knaak}) 11. Qxb7 N8c6 12. Bf4 Nc2+ 13. Kd2 Nxa1 14. Rxa1 Bf6 15. Rd1 Bxc3+ 16. bxc3 Qf6 17. Bh3 d5 18. Bg5 Qg6 19. Ke1 $16 {1-0 Gajewski,G-Hernandez Carmenates,H/Calvia 2006/EXT 2007 (32)}) (9... Na6!? {but in the following game Black failed to equalize:} 10. Nh4 d6 11. Nf5 Re8 12. O-O Bf8 13. a3 Bc8 14. Rb1 Nc7 15. b4 $14 Bxf5 16. Qxf5 g6 17. Qc2 Nd7 18. Bf4 $14 {1-0 Tregubov,P-Hernandez Carmenates,H/Merida MEX 2007/The Week in Chess 685 (60)}) 10. Nxd5 Nxd5 11. Nh4 (11. O-O!? {[%cal Yf1d1]}) 11... Nb4 12. Qd2 N8c6 13. Nf5 Nd4! {[%mdl 512] This exchange sacrifice solves Black's problems. Although he gets doubled pawn with it, his pieces occupy strong squares in the centre.} 14. Nxd4 cxd4 15. Bxa8 Qxa8 16. O-O Qe4 17. a3 (17. f3 Qg6) 17... Nc2 18. Ra2 Rc8 {[%csl Gc2]} 19. b3 Rc3 20. Bb2 Rc6 21. Rd1 Bf6 22. Qd3 (22. Rc1 $145 ! {(Aronian according to Schach 4/2008)}) 22... d5 {[%csl Ge4]} 23. Qf3 (23. Bc1 Rc3 24. Qb5 d3! 25. exd3 Qe6 $44 {[%cal Yc2d4]}) 23... h6 24. h4 g5 25. hxg5 hxg5 26. b4 Kg7 27. Qd3 b5 28. Bc1 (28. Bc1 Rc3! 29. Qxe4 (29. Qxb5 d3! 30. Rxc2 (30. exd3 Qf3 31. Rf1 Rc8 $19) 30... dxc2 31. Rxd5 a6! 32. Rxg5+ $8 Bxg5 33. Qxg5+ Qg6 $15) 29... dxe4 $44) 1/2-1/2

