1. Nf3 c5 2. c3 Nf6 3. d4 e6 4. Bg5 d5 5. e3 h6 6. Bh4 Nc6 7. Nbd2 a6 {A rare move, not very useful for Black. Jeffery Xiong probably wanted to avoid theoretical lines} (7... Be7) ({or} 7... Bd6) 8. Bd3 Be7 9. O-O Nd7 $146 (9... b5 {is premature:} 10. dxc5 Bxc5 11. b4 Be7 12. a4 bxa4 13. Qxa4 Bb7 14. Ne5 Qc8 15. Ndf3 (15. Nxc6!? Bxc6 16. Bxa6) 15... O-O 16. Rfc1 Qc7 17. Bg3 Nxe5 18. Bxe5 Bd6 19. Bxf6 gxf6 20. c4 $14 {1-0 (43) Gausel,E (2490)-Djurhuus,R (2495) Gausdal 1995}) 10. Bxe7 {This exchange makes Black's development task easier.} (10. Bg3!? {looks more logical.}) 10... Nxe7 {Looks like an unnatural recapture but} (10... Qxe7 {is met with} 11. e4! dxe4 $140 12. Bxe4 O-O 13. Re1 {[%cal Ge1e7] , and Black's queen becomes vulnerable on e7.}) 11. Ne5 {Hardly a good continuation but after, say,} (11. a4 b6 {[%cal Yc8b7] White has no plus whatsoever.}) 11... cxd4?! (11... Nxe5 $142 ! 12. dxe5 Nc6 13. Qg4 (13. f4 {loses a pawn after} c4 14. Bc2 Qb6) 13... Qg5! 14. Qxg5 hxg5 15. f4 gxf4 16. exf4 Bd7 $11) 12. exd4 Nxe5 13. dxe5 Bd7 14. Re1 $14 {Now we have a typical position, slighly superior for White due to his better bishop.} Rc8 {Black starts a pawn attack on the queenside; however, it is too slow.} (14... Qb6 15. Rb1 O-O 16. Nf3 f5 17. exf6 Rxf6 {is probably better. Black weakens the e5-square and the e6-pawn but activates his pieces.}) 15. Nf3 b5 16. h4 a5 17. a3 Qb6 18. Qd2 b4?! ({In the event of} 18... O-O {Black's king can easily come under attack:} 19. Re3 {then h4-h5, possibly d3-c2 and d2-d3 etc. But the pawn sacrifice is clearly incorrect.}) 19. cxb4 axb4 20. a4 {White declines the offer and prefers to attack Black's king.} ({Magnus Carlsen was probably unsure of the endgame after} 20. Qxb4 Qxb4 21. axb4 Nc6 (21... Rb8 $143 22. Rec1 Kd8 23. b5 $18) 22. Rec1 Ke7 23. b5 Nb4 24. Bf1 Rxc1 25. Rxc1 Rc8 26. Rxc8 Bxc8 27. Nd4 {. It should be winning, though.}) 20... Ra8 21. b3 O-O 22. Rac1 Rfc8 23. h5?! {Premature.} (23. Nd4 $16 {, stopping Black's counterplay, is more accurate.}) (23. Bb5 Bxb5 24. Qxb4 {is less clear due to} Rab8 25. Qxe7 (25. Rxc8+ Nxc8) 25... Bd3 26. Rxc8+ Rxc8 27. b4 Rc2 28. Re3 Bg6 $132) 23... Kf8?! {Missing} (23... Rc3! 24. Rxc3 bxc3 25. Qxc3 Rc8 {Black regains the pawn with good drawing chances.}) 24. g4?! ({Here} 24. Bb5! Bxb5 25. Qxb4 {was very strong. White won a pawn without any compensation. The text move, continuing White's kingside assault, is less convincing.}) 24... Rc3 {(a bit late)} 25. g5 {[%mdl 128]} hxg5 (25... Nf5! {was a better defence although Black's position remained dangerous.}) 26. Rxc3 bxc3 27. Qxg5 Nf5 (27... Ng8 28. Kh1 {[%cal Ye1g1]} Qd8 29. Qg3 $40) 28. Bxf5 exf5 29. e6! Bxe6 30. h6! gxh6 31. Qf6 Kg8?? {[%mdl 8192] This error leads to an immediate defeat but after} (31... Qd8! 32. Qxc3! {White retains strong pressure anyway.}) 32. Qxh6 {[%cal Rg1h1] Unexpectedly, Black has no defence.} Qb4 33. Kh1 1-0

