1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Nc3 g6 4. d4 cxd4 5. Nxd4 Bg7 6. Be3 Nf6 7. Bc4 O-O 8. Bb3 e6!? ({An interesting atempt to take advantage of the presence of the d-pawn on its initial square.} 8... d6 {would have transposed to a genuine Dragon.}) 9. O-O d5 10. exd5 Nxd5 11. Nxd5 exd5 12. c3 Na5 {new} 13. Qd3 Nxb3 14. axb3 a6 15. Qd2 Re8 16. Rfe1 Bd7 17. Nc2 Bc6 18. Bd4 f6! {Optically speaking, an "ugly" move, creating a weakness and restricting the own bishop. However, this is the lesser evil in this position. Allowing the exchange of the dark-squared bishops would have left Black's position in ruins.} 19. Rxe8+ Qxe8 20. h3 Qf7 21. Nb4 Bf8 22. Nxc6 bxc6 23. b4 Bd6 24. b5 cxb5 25. Bxf6 a5 26. Bd4 Qf4 27. Qxf4 1/2-1/2

