1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 e6 4. Bxc6 bxc6 5. d3 Ne7 6. Qe2 Qc7 7. Ng5 e5 8. f4 exf4 9. O-O Ng6 10. Qh5 d6 {Carlsen has done his homework and studied this interesting line in some detail. We will have to wait till somebody decides to test 10...e5!? with an unpleasant pin for the white queen.} (10... Bd6 11. g3 Ba6?! (11... fxg3! 12. Rxf7 gxh2+ 13. Kh1 Ba6 14. Nxh7 Kxf7 15. Qf5+ Ke8 16. Qxg6+ Kd8 17. Qxg7 Be5 18. Nf6 Kc8 19. Qxh8+ Kb7 20. Qh6 Bxf6 21. Bf4 Qd8 22. e5 Qg8 23. Nc3 Qg4 {0-1 Cornette,M (2482)-Palac,M (2571)/Dresden 2007 (27)}) 12. gxf4 Rf8 13. e5 Be7 14. Nc3 O-O-O 15. Nge4 f5 16. Ng5 Bxg5 17. Qxg5 d6 18. Be3 dxe5 19. fxe5 Qxe5 20. Rae1 $16 {1-0 Bologan,V (2679)-Lautier,J (2676)/Reykjavik 2004 (46)}) (10... Qe5!? 11. Bxf4 (11. Nd2 h6 12. Ndf3 Qf6 $13) 11... Qd4+ (11... Qxb2 12. Na3 Qd4+ (12... Qxa3? 13. Nxf7) 13. Kh1 h6 $13) 12. Kh1 Qf6! 13. e5 Qf5 14. Qf3 Nxf4 15. Qxf4 Qxf4 16. Rxf4 f6 $15) 11. Bxf4 Nxf4! (11... h6?! 12. Nxf7! Qxf7 13. Bxd6 Qe6 14. Bxf8 Rxf8 15. Nd2 Bd7 16. Qxc5 Qe7 17. Rxf8+ Kxf8 18. Rf1+ Kg8 19. Qxe7 Nxe7 20. Nb3 Rd8 21. Nc5 {1-0 Grischuk,A (2710)-Shirov,A (2720)/Moscow 2006 (51)}) (11... f6 12. Nf3 (12. Nxh7 Qf7 13. Bg3 Be6 14. Nd2 O-O-O) 12... Qf7 13. Bg3 Ne5 14. Qxf7+ $14) 12. Rxf4 g6 13. Qf3 (13. Qh4? h6! 14. Nxf7 (14. Rf6 Be7 15. Rxf7 Bxg5 $19) 14... Rh7! 15. Qg3 g5! 16. Nxg5 hxg5 17. Qxg5 Qg7 $19) 13... Bg7! (13... Bh6? 14. Rxf7 Qa5 15. Nd2 (15. Nc3 Bxg5 16. Rf1 Be6 17. Rf6! (17. e5 d5 18. Rf6! $16) 17... Kd7 18. Rxe6! Raf8 (18... Kxe6 19. Qf7+) 19. Rxd6+ Kxd6 20. Qg3+ $16) 15... Bxg5 (15... Qxd2 16. Qf6 Bxg5 17. Re7+ Kd8 18. Qxd6+ $18) 16. Nc4 Qd8 17. e5 Bg4 (17... dxe5 18. Re1 Bf5 19. Nxe5 $18) 18. Qf2 dxe5 19. Re1 Bf5 20. Nxe5 $18) 14. Rxf7 (14. e5?! O-O! (14... Bxe5?? 15. Rxf7 Qd8 16. Qxc6+ $18) 15. exd6 Qd8 (15... Qxd6 16. Nd2 Qe5 $17) 16. Nxf7 Qe8! $19) (14. Nd2!? O-O 15. Rf1 f6 16. Nc4 Rb8 $15) 14... Bd4+ {Both young players must have known some interesting analyses of this sharp position. Each move required attention and exact calculation.} 15. Kh1 (15. Kf1!? Qd8 16. Nxh7 Bf5! (16... Qh4 17. c3 Rxh7 18. Rxh7 Qxh7 19. cxd4 Qh6 20. Na3 Qxh2 21. Re1 $16) 17. Rf8+ Rxf8 18. Nxf8 Bg4 19. Qxg4 Qf6+ 20. Qf3 Qxf3+ 21. gxf3 Bxb2 $15) 15... Qd8! 16. c3 (16. Rxh7 Rxh7 17. Nxh7 Bxb2 18. e5 Qe7!! 19. Qxc6+ Kd8 20. Qxa8 Qxh7 $17) (16. Nd2 Qxg5 17. Nc4 Be5 18. Rf1 Be6 $17) (16. Nxh7!? Bf5 (16... Bxb2? 17. Nc3! Bxa1 (17... Bxc3 18. Rf1 Bf5 19. exf5 Kxf7 20. fxg6+ Kg7 21. Qf7+ Kh6 22. Rf3 $18) 18. Rf8+ Rxf8 19. Qxf8+ Kd7 20. Qf7+ Qe7 21. Nf6+ Kd8 22. Qg8+ Kc7 23. Ncd5+ cxd5 24. Nxd5+ Kd7 25. Nxe7 Kxe7 26. g4 $16) (16... Be6!? 17. Rf8+ Rxf8 18. Qxf8+ Kd7 19. Qxd8+ Rxd8 20. Nc3 $14) (16... Qh4? 17. Rf8+ Rxf8 18. Qxf8+ Kd7 19. Nd2 $18) 17. Rxf5 gxf5 (17... Qe7? 18. Nf6+ Kd8 19. Ng8! Rxg8 20. Rf7 $16) 18. Qh5+ Kd7 19. Qxf5+ Kc7 20. Ng5 Rh6!? 21. Nd2 Qg8 $15) 16... Be5 {After the game it seems, that White is the one playing with fire. There is a strong suspicion, that Black could have tried for an advantage with 16...xg5!?} (16... Qxg5!? 17. cxd4 Qc1+ (17... Bf5 18. Nc3! Kxf7 19. exf5 $44) 18. Qf1 Qxf1+ 19. Rxf1 cxd4 20. Nd2 Ba6 21. Nc4 Ke7 $17) 17. Rg7? (17. d4? cxd4 18. cxd4 Bxd4 19. Rxh7 Rxh7 20. Nxh7 Qe7! (20... Bxb2?! 21. Nc3! Bxa1 22. Qf8+ Kd7 23. Qf7+ Qe7 24. Nf6+ Kd8 25. Qg8+ Kc7 26. Ncd5+ cxd5 27. Nxd5+ Kd7 28. Nxe7 Rb8 29. h4 Kxe7 $13) 21. Nd2 Qxh7 $19) (17. h4! h6 18. Rg7! Rf8 (18... Qf6 19. Qxf6 Bxf6 20. Rxg6 $14) 19. Rf7 (19. Rg8!? Qe7 20. Rxf8+ Qxf8 21. Qxf8+ Kxf8 22. Nf3 Ba6 $11) 19... Rh8 $11) 17... Qf6! {[%mdl 4] An extremely charming refutation of White's spirited attack, as castling short on move 19 will create a mating attack!} (17... Qxg5? 18. Qf7+ Kd8 19. Qc7+ $11) (17... Rf8? 18. Rg8! $16) 18. Qxf6 (18. Rxh7 Rxh7 19. Nxh7 Qh4 (19... Qh8!? 20. d4 cxd4 21. cxd4 Bxd4 22. Nd2 Qxh7 $17) 20. Qf8+ Kd7 21. Qf7+ Kd8 22. g3 Bxg3 23. Qf6+ Qxf6 24. Nxf6 Be5 25. Nh7 Rb8 $19) 18... Bxf6 19. Rxh7 O-O! 20. Na3 (20. Rh6? Bxg5 21. Rxg6+ Kh7 22. Rxg5 Rf1#) 20... Bxg5 21. Rc7 Rf7 {Carlsen already had a pleasant choice. His only task is to coordinate pieces and punish his unfortunate opponent.} (21... Ba6 22. Nc4 (22. Rxc6 Bxd3 23. Rxd6 Bxe4 $19) 22... Bxc4 23. dxc4 Rf2 24. Rxc6 Raf8 $19) 22. Rxc6 Bf4! 23. Nc4 Bd7 24. Ra6 (24. Rc7? d5 $19) 24... Bb5 25. Ra5 Bxc4 26. dxc4 Be5 27. Rd1 (27. Kg1 Raf8 28. Rb1 Rf2 29. Rxa7 Re2 $19) 27... Raf8 28. g3 Rf2 {Black is dominating the board and thus can play for a mating attack.} 29. b4 (29. Rb5 Re2 $19) 29... Bxc3 30. Rxa7 Bd4 31. Rd7 Rxa2 32. bxc5 Rff2! (32... dxc5 33. Rb1 Bg7 (33... Rff2 34. Rb8+) 34. Kg1 Rc2 $19) 33. Rd8+ (33. Rxd4 Rf1#) 33... Kg7 34. Rd7+ Kh6 0-1

